(function(){
'use strict';
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const Q=(s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType='meaning')=>({s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:`Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/${w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')}`});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistake,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(contexts)?contexts:[contexts],mistakes:[mistake],quiz:qs.map((q,i)=>({id:w+'.q'+(i+1),senseId:w+'.s'+q.s,prompt:q.prompt,answer:q.answer,options:[q.answer,q.wrong1,q.wrong2],explain:q.explain,errorType:q.errorType,type:'辨义与用法'}))});
P('snare','Snare comes from Old English snearu, “noose or snare,” from a Germanic source; it names a loop trap and the act of trapping or entangling someone.',[C('snare.s1','wildlife','The ranger found a wire snare beside the hedge and removed it before the rabbits returned.','护林员在树篱旁发现一个金属丝套索，在兔子回来前把它拆掉了。','wire snare beside the hedge','snare 作名词指套住动物的绳圈或金属丝圈。','The first sense is a loop of wire or rope set to catch an animal.','第一义是用来捕捉动物的绳索或金属丝圈套。'),C('snare.s2','fraud','The fake invoice was designed to snare small suppliers into paying a fee they did not owe.','这张假发票企图诱使小供应商落入圈套，缴纳并不欠的费用。','snare suppliers into paying','snare 作动词比喻让人落入困境或骗局。','The verb can mean trick or trap a person in a bad situation.','动词引申为诱骗某人陷入困境。')],M('A wire snare caught the rabbit by giving it a clear escape route with no loop around it.','A wire snare caught the rabbit by tightening its loop around the animal.','没有套圈且能轻易逃脱的装置并不是用来捕捉动物的 snare。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the ranger remove?','a loop trap set to catch rabbits','a warning sign about foxes','a rabbit-proof fence','The noun snare is a loop of wire or rope used to catch an animal.'),Q(2,'What did the fake invoice try to do?','trap suppliers into an unfair payment','help them cancel a fee','teach them how to set a rabbit trap','The verb sense means deceive or entangle someone in trouble.'),Q(1,'Which object is literally a snare?','a rope loop that closes around an animal','a wide open gate','a cage with no closing mechanism','The loop is the defining feature of this trap.'),Q(2,'To snare a buyer in a scam is to…','draw the buyer into a harmful scheme','release the buyer from an agreement','show the buyer a wildlife photograph','The figurative verb means trap someone in a bad situation.')]);
P('snarl','Snarl is recorded in English for an animal’s angry growl and for tangled threads; its deeper history is uncertain. The verb also means become or make tangled.',[C('snarl.s1','animals','The fox gave a warning snarl when the dog came too close to its den.','狗靠近狐狸的窝时，狐狸发出警告性的低吼。','gave a warning snarl','snarl 作可数名词指动物露齿发出的低沉愤怒声。','The first noun sense is a deep angry sound made by an animal.','第一名词义是动物发出的低沉愤怒声。'),C('snarl.s2','objects','A snarl of charging cables had formed behind the desk and took ten minutes to untangle.','桌子后面缠成了一团充电线，花了十分钟才解开。','snarl of charging cables','a snarl of + 复数名词指难以拆开的缠结团。','The second noun sense is a twisted mass or a state of confusion.','第二名词义指缠结的一团，也可指混乱。'),C('snarl.s3','objects','The wet wool snarled around the spindle as the wheel turned too quickly.','纺车转得太快，湿羊毛便缠在纱锭上。','snarled around the spindle','snarl 作动词表示线、毛发等缠结在一起。','The verb means become tangled or make something into a tight tangle.','动词表示缠结，或使东西缠成一团。')],M('The charging cables formed a snarl because each one lay straight, separate, and easy to follow.','The charging cables formed a snarl because they twisted together behind the desk.','分开且笔直的线缆不构成难解的缠结。','context'),[Q(1,'What sound did the fox make?','a deep angry growl','a quiet sneeze','a musical bird call','A snarl can be an animal’s low, angry sound.'),Q(2,'What was behind the desk?','a tangled mass of cables','a wire loop for rabbits','a single straight cord','A snarl can name a difficult tangle.'),Q(3,'What happened to the wool?','it twisted around the spindle','it was cut off in one quick movement','it was used to trap a fox','The verb snarl means become tangled.'),Q(2,'Which phrase uses snarl as a noun for confusion?','a snarl of cables','the dog snarled','she snarled at him','The “snarl of” construction names a twisted mass.')]);
P('snatch','Snatch is recorded from Middle English for a sudden grasp or seizure; its deeper origin is uncertain. The verb can mean seize quickly, grab a short opportunity, or name a brief portion.',[C('snatch.s1','theft','A thief snatched the phone from the cyclist’s basket and ran into the alley.','小偷从骑车人的车筐里抢走手机，跑进了小巷。','snatched the phone','snatch 作及物动词表示迅速、常带强力地夺取。','The first sense is to take something quickly, often by force.','第一义是迅速拿走，常带有强夺意味。'),C('snatch.s2','time','During the layover, she snatched twenty minutes of sleep in a chair near the gate.','转机等候时，她在登机口附近的椅子上抓紧睡了二十分钟。','snatched twenty minutes of sleep','snatch time/sleep 表示时间有限时赶快获得一点。','The second sense is do or get something quickly because there is little time.','第二义是时间不多时赶快做或得到一点。'),C('snatch.s3','fragment','The documentary gave viewers only a snatch of the interview before cutting to the next scene.','纪录片只给观众看了一小段采访，随后就切到了下一个场景。','a snatch of the interview','a snatch of + 内容表示很短的一段。','The noun can mean a short part of something, or an act of snatching.','名词也可指某事的一小段。')],M('The thief snatched the phone by leaving it untouched in the basket and walking away empty-handed.','The thief snatched the phone by grabbing it quickly from the basket.','完全没拿走手机就不符合 snatch“迅速夺取”的动作。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the thief do?','grabbed the phone quickly, likely by force','borrowed it after asking permission','left it in the basket','Snatch means take something suddenly and often forcibly.'),Q(2,'What did she manage during the layover?','a brief period of sleep','a full night’s rest','a short part of the interview','To snatch time is to fit in a little when time is limited.'),Q(3,'How much of the interview did viewers see?','a short fragment','the entire unedited conversation','no recorded material at all','A snatch can be a short piece of something.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses snatch in the “seize” sense?','He snatched the envelope before it fell.','She snatched an hour to read.','The film showed a snatch of the debate.','The first use describes a quick physical taking.')]);
P('sneak','Sneak is recorded from Scots and Northern English in the 16th century; its deeper origin is uncertain. It means move secretly, take or do something secretly, or (dated/derogatory) an informer.',[C('sneak.s1','movement','The child sneaked down the stairs after bedtime so she would not wake her brother.','孩子睡觉后悄悄下楼，以免吵醒弟弟。','sneaked down the stairs','不及物 sneak 表示安静、隐蔽地移动。','The first sense is to go somewhere quietly so nobody sees you.','第一义是悄悄走到某处，不让人看见。'),C('sneak.s2','secrecy','He sneaked a quick look at the answer sheet before the papers were collected.','试卷收走前，他偷偷瞄了一眼答案纸。','sneaked a quick look','sneak + object 表示偷偷做某事或把某物带到某处。','The second sense is take or do something secretly.','第二义是秘密地做某事或偷偷拿带某物。'),C('sneak.s3','informal','The children called him a sneak after he reported their harmless prank to the head teacher.','他把孩子们无伤大雅的恶作剧报告给校长后，孩子们叫他告密者。','called him a sneak','名词 sneak 在此为旧式、贬义的告密者。','The noun can mean an informer, especially in dated or disapproving use.','名词义可指告密者，常带旧式或贬义色彩。')],M('He sneaked down the stairs by switching on every light and announcing each step to his brother.','He sneaked down the stairs quietly so his brother would not notice him.','大声宣布并开灯与偷偷安静行动相反。','context'),[Q(1,'Why did the child sneak downstairs?','to move without waking her brother','to tell the head teacher about a prank','to take an answer sheet','Sneak as a verb means move secretly and quietly.'),Q(2,'What did he secretly do?','looked at the answer sheet','reported the children to the head teacher','walked loudly down the stairs','Sneak can mean do something secretly.'),Q(3,'Why were the children annoyed with him?','they saw him as an informer','he had moved quietly','he had taken a short nap','A sneak as a noun can be a person who informs on others.'),Q(1,'Which is the quiet movement sense?','She sneaked out before the meeting ended.','She sneaked a biscuit into her bag.','They called him a sneak.','Only the first describes moving secretly.')]);
P('sneaker','Sneaker is sneak + -er; the American term for a rubber-soled athletic shoe arose because such shoes let people move quietly.',C('sneaker.s1','clothing','He packed a pair of sneakers with rubber soles for the long walk across campus.','他为穿过校园的长途步行装了一双橡胶底运动鞋。','a pair of sneakers','美式英语常用 sneaker 指休闲或运动鞋。','A sneaker is a casual athletic shoe, usually with a rubber sole.','sneaker 是通常有橡胶底的休闲运动鞋。'),M('She packed sneakers for the hike, choosing stiff metal-soled boots that could not bend or grip the trail.','She packed sneakers for the hike, choosing flexible athletic shoes with rubber soles.','刚硬金属底靴不是通常所说的轻便橡胶底 sneakers。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What footwear did he pack?','casual athletic shoes with rubber soles','formal leather dress shoes with heels','a pair of snowshoes','Sneakers are usually casual athletic shoes with rubber soles.'),Q(1,'Why is the word sneaker linked to sneak?','rubber-soled shoes allowed quiet movement','the shoe was designed for catching rabbits','it was first a type of snowdrift','The name is associated with moving quietly in soft-soled footwear.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural in American English?','a pair of sneakers for the walk','a sneaker of soup','a sneaker of six','Sneaker is a common American word for an athletic shoe.'),Q(1,'What feature is typical of a sneaker?','a flexible rubber sole','a metal loop trap','a pointed animal snout','The source sense describes a casual athletic shoe with rubber sole.')]);
P('sneaky','Sneaky is sneak + -y, an adjective for behavior that hides a sly or dishonest purpose.',C('sneaky.s1','deception','The bill included a sneaky service fee in tiny print that the salesperson had never mentioned.','账单用小字列了一项狡猾的服务费，销售员此前从未提过。','sneaky service fee','形容词修饰 fee，强调费用被隐蔽地加入。','Sneaky describes something done to hide a sly or dishonest purpose.','sneaky 指遮掩狡猾或不诚实目的的行为。'),M('The fee was sneaky because it was clearly listed in large print and explained before purchase.','The fee was sneaky because it was hidden in tiny print and not disclosed before purchase.','充分醒目披露与隐蔽收费的 sneaky 特征相反。','context'),[Q(1,'Why was the service fee sneaky?','it was hidden in tiny print and not disclosed','it was openly explained before purchase','it paid for a rubber sole','Sneaky suggests concealment of a sly purpose.'),Q(1,'Which action is sneaky?','secretly adding an undisclosed charge','posting all prices clearly','asking permission before borrowing','The adjective describes hidden, dishonest conduct.'),Q(1,'What is the base of sneaky?','sneak','snack','snout','Sneaky is formed from sneak with -y.'),Q(1,'A sneaky plan is likely…','designed to hide what the planner is doing','fully transparent to everyone','a neutral description of a snowstorm','The word signals slyness or concealment.')]);
P('sneer','Sneer is recorded in English from Dutch/Low German-related forms, with its precise path uncertain; it means show contempt by a scornful expression or remark.',[C('sneer.s1','reaction','The reviewers sneered at the proposal instead of explaining which evidence they found weak.','评论者没有说明证据哪里薄弱，而是对提案嗤之以鼻。','sneered at the proposal','sneer at + 对象表示用表情或话语轻蔑对待。','The verb means show scorn through a twisted smile or contemptuous words.','动词表示用撇嘴或轻蔑言语表达瞧不起。'),C('sneer.s2','expression','A sneer crossed his face when the apprentice asked a basic question.','学徒问了一个基础问题时，他脸上掠过一丝冷笑。','a sneer crossed his face','名词指表达轻蔑的神情或话语。','The noun is a look or remark that expresses contempt.','名词是表达轻蔑的神情或话语。')],M('The reviewer sneered at the proposal by praising its careful evidence and treating the author with respect.','The reviewer sneered at the proposal with a contemptuous smile and dismissive words.','赞扬证据并尊重作者并不是 sneer 所表示的轻蔑态度。','meaning'),[Q(1,'How did the reviewers respond?','with contempt rather than a reasoned critique','by carefully praising the evidence','by quietly falling asleep','Sneer means show scorn, often through words or expression.'),Q(2,'What crossed his face?','a contemptuous look','a wire snare','a snowflake','A sneer as a noun is a look or remark expressing contempt.'),Q(1,'Which phrase takes the common preposition?','sneer at an idea','sneer in an idea','sneer from an idea','The verb commonly takes at before its target.'),Q(2,'Which is a sneer?','a curled, contemptuous smile','a sincere thank-you','a sneeze into a tissue','The noun describes an expression of scorn.')]);
P('sneeze','Sneeze is recorded in Middle English with an altered initial consonant; its earlier form was fnesen, and its deeper Germanic history is uncertain.',C('sneeze.s1','health','Dust from the old curtain made Lina sneeze twice, so she opened a window and reached for a tissue.','旧窗帘上的灰尘让莉娜打了两个喷嚏，于是她开窗并拿了张纸巾。','made Lina sneeze','sneeze 作动词表示突然把气从鼻腔和口腔喷出。','To sneeze is to expel air suddenly and noisily through the nose and mouth.','sneeze 指突然、出声地从鼻腔和口腔喷气。'),M('The dust made Lina sneeze by causing her to inhale quietly without expelling any air.','The dust made Lina sneeze by triggering a sudden noisy burst of air through her nose and mouth.','只安静吸气而没有突然喷气，不是打喷嚏。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the dust cause Lina to do?','expel air suddenly through her nose and mouth','sniff a cable','speak in a low growl','Sneeze is the sudden, noisy expulsion of air.'),Q(1,'What did Lina reach for after sneezing?','a tissue','a wire snare','a snow board','The example links the sneeze to wiping the nose.'),Q(1,'Which action is a sneeze?','a sudden “achoo” burst after dust irritates the nose','a slow sip of water','a scornful smile','The verb describes the characteristic sudden burst of air.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses sneeze correctly?','The pepper made him sneeze.','The pepper sneezed the saucepan.','He sneezed the pepper into a snare.','A irritant can make a person sneeze.')]);
P('snide','Snide appeared in English slang in the 19th century; its origin is uncertain. It describes an indirect, sneering criticism meant to hurt.',C('snide.s1','conversation','Her snide comment about the intern’s clothes embarrassed him, though she framed it as a joke.','她挖苦实习生衣着的话让他很难堪，尽管她把话说成玩笑。','snide comment about','snide 修饰 comment，指出话语间接却带有伤人讥讽。','Snide means containing indirect but hurtful sneering criticism.','snide 指含有间接但存心伤人的讥讽。'),M('His snide remark was a warm, direct compliment that made the intern feel respected.','His snide remark was an indirect, hurtful criticism disguised as a joke.','真诚赞美不会构成 snide 的挖苦。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did the comment feel snide?','it criticized the intern indirectly to hurt him','it praised him directly','it described a snowstorm','Snide is indirect but deliberately hurtful criticism.'),Q(1,'Which sentence is snide?','“You did surprisingly well for someone new,” she said with a smirk.','“Thank you for your careful work,” she said warmly.','“The train leaves at six,” he said neutrally.','The first sentence carries a disguised insult.'),Q(1,'What does snide usually describe?','a sneering remark or attitude','a kind sincere apology','an athletic shoe','The adjective characterizes contemptuous criticism.'),Q(1,'Why is a snide joke hurtful?','it disguises a cutting criticism as humor','it makes the speaker genuinely apologize','it removes all negative meaning','Snide remarks often hide the insult behind a joking tone.')]);
P('sniff','Sniff is probably imitative of the sound of drawing air through the nose; it can mean smell by inhaling, make an audible intake to show dislike, or a slight sign.',[C('sniff.s1','smell','The dog sniffed the parcel carefully before its handler opened it.','训导员打开包裹前，狗仔细地嗅了嗅。','sniffed the parcel','sniff at + 物体表示吸气以闻气味。','The first sense is breathe in through the nose to smell something.','第一义是用鼻子吸气闻某物。'),C('sniff.s2','reaction','He sniffed at the proposal and called it beneath the committee’s standards.','他对提议嗤之以鼻，称其不符合委员会的标准。','sniffed at the proposal','sniff at an idea 可表示以轻蔑态度表示不屑。','This sense is an audible intake of breath that can express dislike or contempt.','此义可指表示不喜欢或轻视的吸鼻声。'),C('sniff.s3','sign','There was a sniff of smoke in the hallway, although no flame was visible.','走廊里隐约有一丝烟味，尽管看不到火焰。','a sniff of smoke','a sniff of + 抽象/可感物可指轻微迹象或少量。','The noun can mean a slight sign or a small amount of something.','名词也可指某事的轻微迹象或少量。')],M('The dog sniffed the parcel by keeping its nose away and refusing to breathe in any air.','The dog sniffed the parcel by drawing air through its nose to detect its smell.','sniff 的嗅闻动作必须通过鼻子吸气。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the dog do to the parcel?','inhaled through its nose to smell it','snatched it and ran','made a contemptuous comment','Sniff as a verb can mean smell by breathing in through the nose.'),Q(2,'What did he communicate by sniffing at the proposal?','disdain or dislike','a trace of smoke','a sneeze','Sniff at can be a dismissive reaction.'),Q(3,'What was in the hallway?','a slight trace of smoke','a full fire with visible flames','a snowdrift','A sniff can mean a slight sign or amount.'),Q(1,'Which use is the physical smelling action?','The dog sniffed the parcel.','She sniffed at the suggestion.','There was a sniff of spring.','The first example means inhale to smell.')]);
P('sniffer','Sniffer is sniff + -er; it names a device or trained dog that detects substances by smell.',C('sniffer.s1','security','A sniffer dog checked the luggage belt for explosives before passengers entered the terminal.','旅客进入航站楼前，一只嗅探犬检查了行李传送带上是否有爆炸物。','sniffer dog checked','sniffer 作名词指依靠嗅觉探测物质的装置或受训动物。','A sniffer is a device or trained dog used to detect drugs, gas, or explosives by smell.','sniffer 是靠气味探测毒品、燃气或爆炸物的装置或受训犬。'),M('The sniffer dog checked the luggage by reading the passengers’ printed tickets rather than smelling anything.','The sniffer dog checked the luggage by smelling for explosives.','sniffer dog 的探测方式是嗅觉，不是读票面文字。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What was the sniffer dog looking for?','explosives by smell','a hidden written ticket','a snowflake','A sniffer detects substances using its sense of smell.'),Q(1,'Which item can be a sniffer?','a gas-detection device that identifies a leak by scent','a silent letter in a word','a shoe with a rubber sole','The noun includes a detecting device, not just a dog.'),Q(1,'What does -er indicate in sniffer?','a device or agent that performs the detecting','a past tense','the opposite of sniff','The suffix commonly forms an agent or instrument noun.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is most natural?','a sniffer dog at the luggage belt','a sniffer snowstorm at the airport','a sniffer of six','The collocation names a trained detection dog.')]);
P('sniffish','Sniffish is sniff + -ish, an uncommon adjective suggesting a disdainful, superior manner as if one were sniffing at others.',C('sniffish.s1','attitude','The curator gave a sniffish reply to the local artist, as though the question were beneath her.','策展人轻蔑地回应当地艺术家，仿佛这个问题不值得她认真回答。','sniffish reply','-ish 形成形容词；此处描写带优越感和轻蔑的态度。','Sniffish means disdainful and superior in manner.','sniffish 指态度轻蔑、仿佛高人一等。'),M('The curator’s sniffish reply welcomed the artist as an equal and treated the question with respect.','The curator’s sniffish reply dismissed the artist’s question as unworthy of attention.','平等尊重的回答与 sniffish 的轻蔑优越态度相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What tone did the curator’s reply have?','disdainful and superior','warmly respectful','quietly sleepy','Sniffish describes a superior, dismissive manner.'),Q(1,'Which response sounds sniffish?','“I suppose that is the best a local artist could manage,” she said.','“That is a thoughtful question; let us examine it.”','“The gallery opens at six.”','The first reply carries condescending contempt.'),Q(1,'How is sniffish formed?','sniff + -ish','snow + -fall','snip + -er','The adjective adds -ish to sniff.'),Q(1,'A sniffish answer implies the speaker thinks…','the questioner is beneath serious attention','everyone is equally welcome','the room is too cold','The adjective signals disdain and superiority.')]);
P('snip','Snip is imitative of the short sound of scissors closing; as a noun it is one quick cut or the small piece cut off, and as a verb it means cut with short movements.',[C('snip.s1','craft','The seamstress removed the loose thread with one neat snip of her scissors.','裁缝用剪刀利落地剪了一下，去掉了松脱的线头。','one neat snip','snip 作名词表示一次短促剪切动作。','The first noun sense is one quick cutting action or a small piece cut away.','第一名词义是一次短促剪切，或剪下的小段。'),C('snip.s2','cooking','Snip the chive stems into short pieces over the bowl just before serving.','上桌前把细香葱茎剪成小段，直接剪到碗里。','Snip the chive stems','祈使句中 snip 作及物动词，表示用剪切动作剪开。','The verb means cut cloth, thread, or similar material with short blade movements.','动词指用短促刀刃动作剪开布、线等。')],M('The seamstress removed the thread with one snip by pulling it gently without cutting it.','The seamstress removed the thread with one snip by cutting it quickly with scissors.','没有剪断而只是拉扯不构成一次 snip。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the seamstress do with one snip?','cut off a loose thread quickly','tied the thread into a knot','sniffed the fabric','A snip is a quick cut or a small cut-off piece.'),Q(2,'How should the chive stems be prepared?','cut into short pieces with scissors','boiled whole for an hour','wrapped in a snare','The verb snip describes short cutting movements.'),Q(1,'Which is a snip as a noun?','a small cut made by scissors','a long uncut length of cloth','a contemptuous smile','The noun can name one short cutting action.'),Q(2,'Which sentence uses snip as a verb?','Snip the ribbon to the required length.','One snip fell onto the table.','The dog gave a snarl.','The first sentence uses snip as an action.')]);
P('snipe','Snipe comes from the name of the wading bird; shooting snipe from cover gave the verb its literal sense, later extended to sudden verbal attacks.',C('snipe.s1','criticism','The columnist sniped at the budget from the sidelines but offered no workable alternative.','专栏作者在一旁冷嘲热讽预算，却没有提出可行替代方案。','sniped at the budget','snipe at + target 表示突然或隐蔽地尖锐批评。','The verb can mean attack someone with sudden criticism, as well as shoot from cover.','动词可指从隐蔽处射击，也可指突然尖锐抨击。'),M('The columnist sniped at the budget by openly praising it and proposing no criticism whatsoever.','The columnist sniped at the budget with sudden, sharp criticism from the sidelines.','公开赞扬不是 sniping；该用法是尖锐的暗中批评。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the columnist do?','made sudden sharp criticisms of the budget','rewrote the budget as a law','snipped a loose thread','Snipe at can mean attack with sudden criticism.'),Q(1,'What is the literal hunting sense of snipe?','shoot a bird from cover','catch a rabbit in a wire loop','smell for explosives','The verb’s original shooting sense relates to hunting the bird.'),Q(1,'Which action is figurative sniping?','posting a barbed attack on a rival without offering a solution','carefully revising a rival’s report','quietly complimenting the rival','The figurative sense is a sudden verbal attack.'),Q(1,'Which preposition is used in “snipe ___ the plan”?','at','under','during','The target is introduced by at in this usage.')]);
P('snippet','Snippet appeared in English in the 15th century as a diminutive of snip; it names a short extract from writing, music, or conversation.',C('snippet.s1','media','The radio played a brief snippet of the interview to introduce the longer programme.','电台播放了一小段采访，为稍后的完整节目作引子。','snippet of the interview','a snippet of + 内容表示从整体中摘出的短片段。','A snippet is a short extract from a text, song, or conversation.','snippet 是文章、歌曲或谈话中的一小段。'),M('The broadcast called the complete two-hour unedited interview a snippet.','The broadcast called a brief extract from the interview a snippet.','完整的两小时访谈不属于短小片段。','measurement'),[Q(1,'What did the radio play?','a brief extract from an interview','the entire two-hour recording','a weather alarm','A snippet is a short extract.'),Q(1,'Which item could be a snippet?','two lines quoted from a long speech','the full speech from beginning to end','a whole three-season television series','Snippet refers to a small part of a larger whole.'),Q(1,'How is snippet related to snip?','it is a diminutive form historically related to snip','it is the plural of snow','it means an animal’s nose','The word developed as a small piece or extract.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a snippet of conversation','a snippet the whole interview completely','a snippet of six feet tall','The noun commonly appears with “of” before the source material.')]);
P('snob','Snob first appeared in English in the 18th century; its origin is uncertain, despite several popular but unproven explanations. It now means someone who overvalues status and looks down on others.',C('snob.s1','attitude','He is a snob about wine and dismisses bottles from small regions without tasting them.','他在葡萄酒方面很势利，连尝都不尝就看不起小产区的酒。','a snob about wine','snob about + subject 表示在某领域摆出势利或优越姿态。','A snob gives too much importance to rank or taste and despises those judged inferior.','snob 过分看重地位或品味，并轻视被认为不如自己的人。'),M('The wine snob welcomed every bottle equally and never judged anyone by price or status.','The wine snob dismissed modest bottles because he thought only prestigious labels were worth drinking.','不按地位或价格轻视他人，不能体现 snob 的势利态度。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why is he a snob about wine?','he dismisses lesser-known bottles without tasting them','he carefully tastes wines from every region','he works at a snowboarding shop','A snob overvalues status and looks down on what seems inferior.'),Q(1,'Which person is a snob?','someone who mocks people for buying inexpensive clothes','someone who treats all customers with equal respect','someone who detects gas leaks','Snob describes status-conscious contempt.'),Q(1,'What is known about the word’s origin?','its exact origin is uncertain','it certainly abbreviates “sine nobilitate”','it comes from the word snowboard','The popular expansion is not established as fact.'),Q(1,'Which phrase fits the source sense?','a snob about social rank','a snob of a snowflake','a snob to sneeze','The noun can name someone with status-based disdain.')]);
P('snobbish','Snobbish is snob + -ish; it describes contempt for people considered lower in status or an affected attempt to seem socially superior.',[C('snobbish.s1','class','The hotel’s snobbish doorman ignored guests who arrived by bus but greeted those in expensive cars.','酒店势利的门卫无视乘公交来的客人，却向开豪车的人问候。','snobbish doorman','形容词指因财富或地位而轻视别人。','The first sense is treating people with less money or education as unimportant.','第一义是认为较不富有或教育程度较低的人不重要。'),C('snobbish.s2','taste','Her snobbish club praised only rare imported teas, pretending ordinary local blends were uncultured.','她那个附庸风雅的俱乐部只夸稀有进口茶，装作普通本地茶没有品味。','snobbish club','此处是借追捧富人偏好的品味来显得更重要。','The second sense is trying to seem important by favoring things associated with the rich.','第二义是追捧富人偏好的东西以显得高人一等。')],M('The doorman’s snobbish policy gave the same warm welcome to every guest regardless of income.','The doorman’s snobbish policy favored wealthy guests and ignored people arriving by bus.','不看身份而平等欢迎所有人不符合势利的区别对待。','context'),[Q(1,'Who was ignored by the doorman?','guests who arrived by bus','guests in expensive cars','members of the hotel staff','The first sense describes status-based disregard.'),Q(2,'Why did the club seem snobbish?','it treated ordinary local tea as inferior to elite imports','it served every tea equally','it disliked all expensive items','The second sense is affected elitism in taste.'),Q(1,'What does -ish contribute to snobbish?','the adjective sense “having the manner of a snob”','a plural form','an action of cutting','The suffix forms an adjective from the noun snob.'),Q(2,'Which behavior is snobbish in the taste sense?','pretending common food is beneath you to appear refined','enjoying a local blend without comparison','helping a guest carry bags','It involves performative superiority around taste.')]);
P('snoop','Snoop may come from Dutch snoepen, “eat secretly,” though the path is uncertain; it means pry into private affairs and can name a meddlesome person.',[C('snoop.s1','privacy','The manager snooped through employees’ desks while they were at lunch, looking for private notes.','员工午餐时，经理翻看他们的办公桌，寻找私人便笺。','snooped through employees’ desks','snoop through + place 表示隐秘或令人反感地窥探私事。','The verb means try to discover private information in a secret or annoying way.','动词指以隐秘或令人反感的方式探听隐私。'),C('snoop.s2','people','The neighbours were snoops, always asking who visited and how long each guest stayed.','邻居们爱打探，老是询问谁来过以及每位客人待了多久。','were snoops','snoop 作名词指爱干涉别人私事的人。','The noun is a person who meddles in others’ private affairs.','名词指窥探他人私事的人。')],M('The manager snooped through the desk by refusing to open it or look at any private papers.','The manager snooped through the desk by secretly searching its private papers.','没有查看或探问任何私事就不能称为 snoop。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What was the manager doing?','prying through private papers','organizing a public meeting','snipping a thread','Snoop is to seek private information in an intrusive way.'),Q(2,'Why were the neighbours called snoops?','they meddled by asking about visitors','they welcomed every guest privately','they repaired the office desks','A snoop is a person who intrudes into others’ affairs.'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses snoop as a verb?','He snooped through her messages.','He is a snoop about everything.','He slept in a chair.','The first sentence describes the intrusive action.'),Q(2,'Which noun is closest to snoop?','a nosy meddler','a trained detection dog','a sports shoe','The noun denotes someone who pries into private matters.')]);
P('snooze','Snooze is an expressive, probably imitative word for sleep; its deeper origin is uncertain. It names a short sleep or the act of taking one.',[C('snooze.s1','rest','After the night shift, Omar took a short snooze in the armchair before driving home.','夜班后，奥马尔在开车回家前于扶手椅上小睡了一会儿。','took a short snooze','take a snooze 是名词搭配，指短暂睡眠。','The noun is a short sleep, often taken during the day.','名词指短暂的小睡，常在白天进行。'),C('snooze.s2','rest','The cat snoozed on the warm step while rain tapped on the roof.','屋顶雨声滴答时，猫在温暖的台阶上打盹。','snoozed on the warm step','snooze 作不及物动词，描述短时睡着。','The verb means spend a short time sleeping, often in the afternoon.','动词表示小睡一会儿。')],M('Omar took a snooze by staying fully awake in the armchair for the entire afternoon.','Omar took a snooze by sleeping briefly in the armchair.','一直清醒不符合 snooze“短暂睡觉”的意思。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did Omar do after his shift?','slept briefly in an armchair','went snowboarding','sniffed for gas','A snooze is a short sleep.'),Q(2,'Where was the cat sleeping?','on a warm step','inside a snare','in a meeting room','Snooze as a verb means take a brief nap.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','take a quick snooze','snatch a snooze into a wire','sneeze a snooze','The noun collocates with take and quick/short.'),Q(2,'Which sentence uses snooze as a verb?','She snoozed after lunch.','She had a snooze after lunch.','The snooze lasted twenty minutes.','Only the first uses snooze as an action.')]);
P('snout','Snout is a Germanic word recorded in Middle English; its exact deeper source is uncertain. It names the projecting front part of an animal’s face, including the mouth.',C('snout.s1','animals','The pig pushed the garden gate with its snout while searching for fallen apples.','猪寻找掉落的苹果时，用口鼻部推开了花园门。','pushed ... with its snout','with 短语说明动物用突出的口鼻部施力。','A snout is the long front part of an animal’s face, with the mouth at the end.','snout 是动物脸部长出的前端，嘴在末端。'),M('The pig opened the gate with its snout, which was the feathered part growing from its back.','The pig opened the gate with its snout, the projecting front of its face around the mouth.','snout 指动物脸部和口鼻部，不是背上的羽毛。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the pig use to push the gate?','the projecting front of its face around its mouth','its tail','a wire loop','Snout is the animal’s front facial part with the mouth at the end.'),Q(1,'Which animal feature is a snout?','a pig’s long nose and mouth area','a bird’s feathered wing','a rabbit’s trap','The word commonly describes pigs, dogs, and similar animals.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','the dog’s wet snout','the dog’s snout of six','the dog snoozed its snout','Snout is a body-part noun.'),Q(1,'What does the source definition emphasize?','the long front part of the face and mouth','a person’s private notes','a short sleep','The snout projects at the front of an animal’s face.')]);
})();

(function(){
'use strict';
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const Q=(s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType='meaning')=>({s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:`Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/${w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')}`});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistake,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(contexts)?contexts:[contexts],mistakes:[mistake],quiz:qs.map((q,i)=>({id:w+'.q'+(i+1),senseId:w+'.s'+q.s,prompt:q.prompt,answer:q.answer,options:[q.answer,q.wrong1,q.wrong2],explain:q.explain,errorType:q.errorType,type:'辨义与用法'}))});
P('snow','Snow is Old English snāw, from Proto-Germanic *snaiwaz; English uses it as both the frozen flakes and the verb for their falling.',[C('snow.s1','weather','Fresh snow covered the footbridge and softened every sound in the pine grove.','新雪覆盖了人行桥，也让松林里的各种声音变得柔和。','fresh snow covered','snow 作名词指寒冷天气下从云中落下的白色冰晶。','The noun names the soft white substance that falls from cold clouds.','名词指寒冷时从云中落下的柔软白色物质。'),C('snow.s2','weather','It snowed steadily through the night, so the morning bus was delayed.','整夜都在持续下雪，因此早班公交晚点了。','It snowed steadily','snow 作天气动词通常不及物，描述雪花降落。','The verb means snow is falling from the sky.','动词指正在下雪。')],M('It snowed all night, so by morning the air was hot and the road was covered with blooming flowers.','It snowed all night, so by morning the road was covered with fresh snow.','整夜降雪的结果通常是积雪，不会自动变成炎热和开花。','context'),[Q(1,'What covered the footbridge?','fresh frozen flakes','a wire trap','a warm blanket','Snow as a noun is the white substance that falls in cold weather.'),Q(2,'What delayed the bus?','snow fell steadily overnight','the snowflake melted in summer','the driver took a snooze','Snow can be used as a verb for falling snow.'),Q(1,'Which is a natural noun use?','The snow blocked the narrow path.','The snowed blocked the path.','The path snows a blanket.','The noun functions as the subject here.'),Q(2,'Which sentence uses snow as a verb?','It may snow before dawn.','The snow lay on the roof.','We brushed snow from the coat.','The first sentence uses the weather verb.')]);
P('snowboard','Snowboard is a compound of snow + board; it names the wide board used to slide on snow and the sport of riding it.',[C('snowboard.s1','equipment','She waxed her snowboard and checked both bindings before the mountain lifts opened.','山地缆车开放前，她给单板打蜡并检查了两个固定器。','waxed her snowboard','名词指双脚固定在其上、在雪面滑行的宽板。','A snowboard is a wide board with both feet fixed on it for sliding over snow.','snowboard 是双脚固定在其上的滑雪宽板。'),C('snowboard.s2','sport','They snowboarded down the beginner slope while an instructor watched from below.','他们在教练从下方看护时沿初级雪道滑单板。','snowboarded down the slope','snowboard 作动词指站在单块宽板上沿雪坡滑行。','The verb means travel down snow slopes standing on one wide board.','动词指站在一块宽板上沿雪坡滑行。')],M('She snowboarded down the slope by fastening one foot to each of two separate skis.','She snowboarded down the slope with both feet fixed to one wide board.','两块独立雪板是滑雪；snowboard 指一块板。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What did she wax?','a single wide board for snow riding','two narrow skis','a wire snare','A snowboard is one wide board used on snow.'),Q(2,'What did the group do on the beginner slope?','rode single boards down the snow','played soccer indoors','snoozed at the lift','The verb snowboard names the sport action.'),Q(1,'How are a rider’s feet secured on a snowboard?','both feet are fixed on one board','one foot is fixed to each of two skis','neither foot touches the board','The equipment is a single wide board.'),Q(2,'Which phrase uses snowboard as a verb?','They snowboarded after lunch.','They repaired a snowboard.','The snowboard is wide.','The first sentence describes the activity.')]);
P('snowdrift','Snowdrift is snow + drift; the compound names snow piled into a mound by wind against an obstacle.',C('snowdrift.s1','weather','A deep snowdrift had built up against the barn door, so the farmer cleared it with a shovel.','谷仓门前被风吹起了一大堆深雪，农夫只好用铲子清除。','snowdrift ... against the barn door','snowdrift 指被风堆在墙、树篱或道路旁的积雪。','A snowdrift is a mound of snow heaped by wind against an obstacle.','snowdrift 是风把雪堆在障碍物旁形成的雪堆。'),M('The farmer called the empty, completely snow-free doorway a deep snowdrift.','The farmer called the wind-heaped mound of snow against the doorway a snowdrift.','没有雪的空门口不可能是雪堆。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What blocked the barn door?','a wind-piled mound of snow','a stack of hay','a snowboard','A snowdrift is a mound heaped by wind.'),Q(1,'Where had the snowdrift formed?','against the barn door','inside the warm kitchen','on the farmer’s snowboard','Snowdrifts build up against obstacles.'),Q(1,'Which feature distinguishes a snowdrift?','snow has been piled by wind','snow is falling evenly from clouds','a person is riding one board','The compound refers to wind-heaped snow.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses snowdrift naturally?','The plow broke through a snowdrift beside the road.','A snowdrift flew high like an eagle.','She placed the snowdrift on her foot.','Snowdrifts are accumulations on the ground.')]);
P('snowfall','Snowfall is the compound snow + fall; it refers to falling snow or the amount received during a period.',C('snowfall.s1','weather records','The weather station recorded a snowfall of twelve centimetres between midnight and sunrise.','气象站记录了午夜至日出期间十二厘米的降雪量。','a snowfall of twelve centimetres','snowfall 可表示降雪本身或一段时间的降雪量。','A snowfall is frozen flakes falling from the sky or the amount that falls in a period.','snowfall 指降雪或一段时间内的降雪量。'),M('The station recorded a snowfall of twelve centimetres, but its gauge showed that no snow had fallen.','The station recorded a snowfall of twelve centimetres after measuring the snow that fell.','降雪量记录应以实际落下的雪为依据。','measurement'),[Q(1,'What did the station measure?','the amount of snow that fell overnight','the depth of the river','the length of a snowboard','Snowfall can mean the quantity of snow during a period.'),Q(1,'Which event is a snowfall?','flakes falling from clouds during a storm','a mound pushed by wind beside a wall','one crystal melting on a sleeve','Snowfall names falling snow or its measured amount.'),Q(1,'What does “heavy snowfall” suggest?','a large amount of snow fell','the snowflake was unusually light','a snowshoe broke','Heavy modifies the amount or intensity of snow.'),Q(1,'Which instrument reading could report snowfall?','12 cm of snow accumulated overnight','12 degrees of room warmth','12 litres of soap','Snowfall is commonly measured as depth or amount.')]);
P('snowflake','Snowflake combines snow + flake; it names one small falling piece of snow, often a branching ice crystal.',C('snowflake.s1','weather','A snowflake landed on her dark sleeve, and its branching crystal pattern vanished as it melted.','一片雪花落在她深色袖子上，分枝状的晶体图案融化后便消失了。','A snowflake landed','可数名词指一片独立的雪晶。','A snowflake is one small piece of falling snow, often with a branching crystal shape.','snowflake 是一小片雪，常呈分枝晶体状。'),M('The child caught a snowflake: a warm liquid drop that had no ice crystal structure.','The child caught a snowflake: a small ice crystal that melted on her glove.','雪花是冰晶而非温热液滴。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What landed on the sleeve?','one small branching ice crystal','a whole snowstorm','a rubber-soled shoe','A snowflake is an individual piece of falling snow.'),Q(1,'Why did the pattern disappear?','the crystal melted','the snowflake turned into a snare','the sleeve became a snowdrift','Snow crystals melt when they warm.'),Q(1,'Which is a snowflake?','a tiny six-sided ice crystal falling from a cloud','a pile pushed against a barn','a month of cold weather','The word names one small piece rather than a storm or mound.'),Q(1,'What does the compound literally combine?','snow and a flake','snow and a board','sniff and a cake','Snowflake is a transparent compound.')]);
P('snowstorm','Snowstorm combines snow + storm; it names severe weather with substantial snowfall, often driven by strong wind.',C('snowstorm.s1','travel','The snowstorm forced the airport to cancel flights until crews cleared the runways.','暴风雪迫使机场取消航班，直到工作人员清理完跑道。','snowstorm forced the airport','名词指大量降雪、常伴强风的恶劣天气。','A snowstorm is severe weather with a large amount of snow, often with wind.','snowstorm 指大量降雪、常伴大风的恶劣天气。'),M('The airport cancelled flights for a snowstorm even though the sky was clear and no snow or wind was present.','The airport cancelled flights during a snowstorm because heavy snow and wind made runways unsafe.','晴朗无雪无风的天气不构成暴风雪。','context'),[Q(1,'Why were flights cancelled?','heavy snow made the runways unsafe','a warm spring breeze melted the snow','the airport ran out of soap','A snowstorm brings severe snowy conditions.'),Q(1,'Which forecast describes a snowstorm?','heavy snow with strong winds','clear skies and mild temperatures','a light shower of warm rain only','Snowstorms involve significant snowfall and often wind.'),Q(1,'What did crews need to clear?','the runways','the snowflake’s crystal branches','the airplane’s software','The storm left snow on airport surfaces.'),Q(1,'How does snowstorm differ from snowfall?','it names a severe weather event, not just falling snow or its amount','it names a single ice crystal','it means a board for sliding','A storm includes the severe conditions around the snow.')]);
P('snowy','Snowy is snow + -y; it describes a place or period with falling/lying snow and, figuratively or by colour, something bright white like new snow.',[C('snowy.s1','weather','We crossed a snowy pass in late January, where drifts still covered the road after the storm.','一月底我们穿过一个多雪的山口，暴风雪后积雪仍覆盖着道路。','snowy pass','snowy 描述正在下雪或地面有积雪的地点、时段。','The first sense describes a place or time when snow is falling or lying on the ground.','第一义指正在下雪或地上有雪的地方或时段。'),C('snowy.s2','appearance','Her snowy white linen stood out against the dark walnut table.','她雪白的亚麻布在深色胡桃木桌上格外醒目。','snowy white linen','snowy 可比喻极浅亮的白色，如新雪。','The second sense means extremely pale and bright like fresh snow.','第二义指像新雪一样明亮洁白。')],M('The snowy linen was described as snowy white even though it was dark brown and dull.','The snowy linen was bright white, like newly fallen snow.','深褐暗淡的布不具备 snowy 的雪白外观。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why was the pass snowy?','snow lay on the road after the storm','it was made of white linen','the road was warm and dry','The first sense describes a snow-covered place or time.'),Q(2,'What did snowy describe about the linen?','its bright white colour','the amount of wind','a snowboarding technique','Snowy can mean pale and bright like fresh snow.'),Q(1,'Which place is snowy in the weather sense?','a mountain road covered in fresh snow','a room with white curtains only','a clear beach in summer','The first sense concerns actual falling or lying snow.'),Q(2,'A snowy-white page is…','extremely bright and pale','made from a snowdrift','covered in muddy brown ink','The appearance sense compares whiteness with snow.')]);
P('snub','Snub is recorded from Old Norse snubba, “to rebuke or check,” though the later social sense developed in English; it can be a deliberate cold dismissal or the act itself.',[C('snub.s1','social','At the reception, the director snubbed the junior researcher by turning away without returning her greeting.','招待会上，主任故意转身不回应初级研究员的问候，冷落了她。','snubbed the junior researcher','snub 作动词表示故意冷淡对待以示不满。','The verb means treat someone with deliberate coldness as a sign of disapproval.','动词指因不满而故意冷淡对待某人。'),C('snub.s2','social','The singer’s failure to thank the local choir was seen as a snub to its members.','歌手没有感谢当地合唱团，被视为对团员们的怠慢。','seen as a snub to','snub 作名词指一次把人当作不重要的冷落行为。','The noun is an act of treating someone as if unimportant.','名词指把某人当作无足轻重的一次举动。')],M('The director snubbed the researcher by warmly greeting her and inviting her to lead the meeting.','The director snubbed the researcher by ignoring her greeting and excluding her from the discussion.','热情回应并邀请主持与故意冷落相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'How did the director snub the researcher?','ignored her greeting and turned away','invited her to lead the meeting','gave her a warm welcome','Snub means deliberately show coldness or disapproval.'),Q(2,'What did the choir interpret as a snub?','the singer’s failure to thank them','the singer’s warm public thanks','the choir’s rehearsal schedule','A snub as a noun is an act of dismissal.'),Q(1,'Which action is a social snub?','refusing to acknowledge someone at a reception','greeting a visitor warmly','asking a colleague for help','The verb describes deliberate cold treatment.'),Q(2,'What does “a snub to the team” mean?','an act that treats the team as unimportant','a snow-covered bench','an official welcome','The noun names the dismissive act.')]);
P('snug','Snug is recorded in English from the late 16th century, probably from Scandinavian or Low German; its exact source is uncertain. It describes warmth and comfort in a small sheltered place.',C('snug.s1','comfort','The cabin felt snug with the stove glowing while rain rattled against the shutters.','炉火明亮、雨点敲打百叶窗时，小木屋里显得温暖舒适。','cabin felt snug','snug 描写狭小而有遮蔽的空间温暖惬意。','Snug means warm and cosy, especially in a small sheltered place.','snug 指在狭小、有遮蔽处感到温暖舒适。'),M('The cabin felt snug because its roof leaked, the stove was cold, and wind blew through every wall.','The cabin felt snug because the warm stove and solid walls sheltered everyone from the rain.','漏雨、无暖炉且四面透风与舒适温暖的 snug 相反。','context'),[Q(1,'Why did the cabin feel snug?','it was warm and sheltered from the rain','it was wide open to wind','the snowstorm had entered the room','Snug describes warm comfort in a sheltered place.'),Q(1,'Which place sounds snug?','a small warm reading nook protected from a draft','an exposed platform in a blizzard','a large empty parking lot','The adjective often describes small cosy spaces.'),Q(1,'What does snug not necessarily mean?','large and exposed','warm and comfortable','sheltered','Snug usually suggests cosy shelter, not openness.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a snug cabin by the stove','a snug blizzard in the sky','a snug of six feet','Snug is an adjective for comfort and warmth.')]);
P('snugly','Snugly is snug + -ly; it means fitting closely and neatly, or being in comfortable warmth.',[C('snugly.s1','fit','The jar lid fits snugly, so the soup will not leak in the lunch bag.','罐盖贴合紧密，因此汤不会漏进午餐袋。','fits snugly','副词修饰 fits，表示盖子紧密而整齐地贴合。','The first sense means closely and neatly.','第一义是贴合紧密而整齐地。'),C('snugly.s1','comfort','The kittens slept snugly together in a basket lined with wool.','小猫们在铺着羊毛的篮子里紧挨着舒适地睡着。','slept snugly together','副词描述温暖舒适地蜷在一起。','The adverb can also describe being in comfortable warmth.','该副词也可表示处于温暖舒适的状态。')],M('The lid fits snugly, leaving a wide gap that lets soup spill into the bag.','The lid fits snugly, leaving no gap for soup to escape.','贴合紧密的盖子不会留下大缝隙。','context'),[Q(1,'How does the lid fit?','closely and neatly','loosely with a wide gap','on the wrong jar','Snugly describes a close, neat fit.'),Q(1,'Where did the kittens sleep?','warmly nestled together in the lined basket','outside in the snowstorm','under a leaking roof','Snugly can mean in comfortable warmth.'),Q(1,'Which use is about fit?','The cap sits snugly on the bottle.','They sat snugly by the fire.','The road was snowy.','The first sentence describes close fitting.'),Q(1,'What did snugly add to “slept together”?','they were comfortable and warmly close','they were loudly snoring','they were separated by a wide gap','The adverb can convey cosy closeness.')]);
P('so','So comes from Old English swā, “in this way, to such a degree”; it functions as an intensifying adverb, a result connector, or a word meaning “also” in inversion.',[C('so.s1','degree','The crate was so heavy that two workers had to lift it together.','箱子太重了，两个工人不得不一起抬。','so heavy that','so + adjective + that 引出程度导致的结果。','The first sense means to such a degree.','第一义表示达到如此程度。'),C('so.s2','result','The bridge was closed, so the buses followed the eastern road.','桥关闭了，因此公交车改走东边的道路。','closed, so the buses','so 连接原因与结果，意为 therefore。','The conjunction means for that reason or therefore.','连词义是“所以、因此”。'),C('so.s3','agreement','Mira likes old maps, and so does her brother.','米拉喜欢旧地图，她弟弟也一样。','and so does her brother','so + auxiliary + subject 表示另一人也如此。','The third use says the same thing is true of another person.','第三种用法表示另一人也一样。')],M('The bridge was closed, so the buses crossed it on their usual route without turning.','The bridge was closed, so the buses took the eastern road instead.','桥关闭是改道原因，不应仍沿桥通过。','context'),[Q(1,'Why did two workers lift the crate?','it was extremely heavy','the bridge was closed','Mira liked old maps','So before heavy marks degree.'),Q(2,'What happened because the bridge closed?','buses used the eastern road','the crate became heavier','Mira learned to read maps','Here so means therefore.'),Q(3,'What does “and so does her brother” mean?','her brother likes old maps too','her brother dislikes maps','her brother closed a bridge','This inverted structure means the same is true of him.'),Q(1,'Which pattern expresses an intense result?','so tired that she fell asleep','so the road is closed','and so did the driver','So + adjective + that introduces the result.')]);
P('so as to','So as to is a purpose phrase built from so + as + to-infinitive; it explains why someone acts in order to achieve a stated result.',C('so as to.s1','purpose','He saved a second copy so as to recover the report if the laptop failed.','他保存了第二份副本，以便电脑故障时恢复报告。','so as to recover','so as to + bare infinitive introduces the intended purpose.','The phrase explains the intended result of an action.','该短语说明做某事是为了达到某个结果。'),M('He saved a second copy so as to lose the report if the laptop failed.','He saved a second copy so as to recover the report if the laptop failed.','保存备份的目的应是恢复文件，而不是让文件丢失。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did he save a second copy?','to recover the report after a laptop failure','to make the laptop fail','to delete both copies','So as to introduces the intended purpose.'),Q(1,'Which form follows so as to?','a base-form verb such as recover','a past-tense verb such as recovered','a noun with no verb','The construction takes a to-infinitive.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses so as to for purpose?','She left early so as to catch the first train.','She left early so as the first train.','She left early so catching the first train.','The phrase is followed by catch, the infinitive.'),Q(1,'What result was the backup meant to make possible?','restoring the report','losing the report','replacing the laptop battery','The example links saving a copy to recovery.')]);
P('so far','So far is the phrase so + far used adverbially for the period from the past up to the present; it often signals that circumstances may still change.',C('so far.s1','progress','We have received three applications so far, but the deadline is still two weeks away.','到目前为止我们收到三份申请，但截止日期还有两周。','three applications so far','句末 so far 与现在完成时连用，表示截至当前的进展。','So far means up to the present time, before a possible change.','so far 表示到目前为止，之后情况仍可能变化。'),M('We have received three applications so far, and the deadline passed a month ago.','We have received three applications so far, and the deadline is still two weeks away.','若截止日期早已过去一个月，就不能把它说成仍有两周。','context'),[Q(1,'How many applications had arrived up to now?','three','none ever','two hundred','So far reports the state up to the present.'),Q(1,'Why might the number change?','the deadline is still in the future','so far means forever','the applications were destroyed','The phrase describes the current state, which may change.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses so far correctly?','No problems have appeared so far.','No problems appeared so far yesterday at noon.','So far is the noun for a snowdrift.','The phrase commonly relates past-to-present time.'),Q(1,'What does so far mean in this update?','up to the present time','far away in distance','for that reason','It gives a temporal status report.')]);
P('so-called','So-called combines so + called, the past participle of call; it can mark a disputed or misleading label, or neutrally introduce a commonly used name.',[C('so-called.s1','skepticism','The so-called “miracle cure” had no clinical evidence and was withdrawn from the advertisement.','这个所谓的“奇迹疗法”没有临床证据，后来从广告中撤下。','so-called “miracle cure”','此处带怀疑语气，暗示名称不准确或有误导性。','The first sense signals that the speaker thinks the name is wrong or misleading.','第一义表示说话者认为该叫法错误或有误导。'),C('so-called.s2','terminology','The so-called greenhouse effect is a well-studied process by which gases retain heat in the atmosphere.','人们称作温室效应的过程，是气体在大气中留住热量的、研究充分的现象。','so-called greenhouse effect','中性用法说明人们通常使用的名称，不一定含批评。','The second sense neutrally introduces a name in common use.','第二义中性地引出人们通常使用的名称。')],M('The so-called “cure” was described as untested, but the speaker used the term to endorse it as a proven treatment.','The so-called “cure” was described as untested, and the speaker questioned whether it deserved that name.','明确称其未经测试并质疑名称，不是在认可其为已证实疗法。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Why is “miracle cure” placed after so-called?','the speaker doubts that the label is accurate','the treatment is proved effective','it is the official name of a snowstorm','The first sense can signal skepticism about a label.'),Q(2,'Is the greenhouse-effect use necessarily critical?','no; it can neutrally state the common name','yes; it always rejects the term','yes; it means the process is fake','The second sense is commonly used without strong criticism.'),Q(1,'Which phrase signals doubt about a title?','the so-called “expert” who offered no evidence','the so-called process, a standard term in textbooks','the expert gave a clear explanation','The first phrase questions whether the title fits.'),Q(2,'Which use is neutral?','the so-called greenhouse effect is the standard term','the so-called expert is a fraud','the so-called cure has no evidence','Neutral so-called introduces the name without rejection.')]);
P('soak','Soak is Old English socian, “to become soaked or steep”; it can mean leave something in liquid, make it very wet, or become thoroughly wet.',[C('soak.s1','preparation','Soak the dried beans overnight in cold water before adding them to the stew.','把干豆放在冷水里浸泡一夜，再加入炖菜。','Soak ... overnight in cold water','soak + object + in liquid 表示将某物放入液体一段时间。','The first sense is put something in liquid for a period of time.','第一义是把某物浸在液体里一段时间。'),C('soak.s2','weather','The sudden downpour soaked the hikers before they found shelter.','徒步者还没找到避雨处，突如其来的大雨就把他们淋透了。','downpour soaked the hikers','soak 作及物动词也可表示使某人或物完全湿透。','The second sense is make something completely wet.','第二义是把某物或某人弄得湿透。')],M('Soak the dried beans overnight by leaving them completely dry in an empty bowl.','Soak the dried beans overnight by covering them with water.','干燥地放置而不接触液体不叫浸泡。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What should happen to the beans overnight?','they should remain in cold water','they should be left dry in a bowl','they should be frozen in snow','To soak something is to leave it in liquid.'),Q(2,'What did the downpour do to the hikers?','made them thoroughly wet','made them fall asleep','trapped them in a snare','Soak can mean make completely wet.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses soak as “steep”?','Soak the lentils before cooking them.','The rain soaked her coat.','Water soaked into the ground.','The first sense leaves an item in liquid for a time.'),Q(2,'What does “We got soaked” mean?','we became completely wet','we soaked beans overnight','we became warmly sheltered','The intransitive/result use describes being drenched.')]);
P('soakage','Soakage is soak + -age, a noun for liquid entering material or the quantity absorbed.',C('soakage.s1','materials','The engineer measured soakage through the clay after each hour of steady rain.','工程师在持续降雨后每隔一小时测量粘土的渗水情况。','measured soakage through the clay','soakage 指液体进入材料的过程或被吸收的量。','Soakage is the action of liquid entering a material, or how much it takes up.','soakage 指液体渗入材料的过程或吸收量。'),M('The clay’s soakage was high because no liquid entered it and none was absorbed.','The clay’s soakage was high because a large amount of water entered and was absorbed.','没有液体进入就不会有高吸收量。','measurement'),[Q(1,'What was measured in the clay?','how much water entered and was absorbed','the clay’s colour','the number of snowflakes','Soakage measures liquid absorption into material.'),Q(1,'Which factor increases soakage?','water moving into porous material','keeping material perfectly dry','polishing a snowboard','Soakage involves liquid entering or being taken up.'),Q(1,'What does -age form in soakage?','a noun naming an action or amount','a comparative adjective','the past form of soak','The suffix forms a process/quantity noun.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses soakage correctly?','The fabric’s soakage was tested with a measured volume of water.','The soakage barked at the door.','She soakage the beans.','The noun refers to an absorption process or amount.')]);
P('soaked','Soaked is the past participle of soak, also used as an adjective for something covered or penetrated by liquid until no part stays dry.',C('soaked.s1','weather','We arrived soaked after waiting for the bus in driving rain without an umbrella.','我们没带伞，在倾盆大雨中等公交，抵达时全身湿透。','arrived soaked','soaked 作表语形容词，说明全身被雨淋湿。','Soaked means covered with liquid until nothing remains dry.','soaked 指被液体浸透、没有一处干燥。'),M('They came in soaked after standing in the rain, but every layer of clothing was perfectly dry.','They came in soaked after standing in the rain, with water through their clothes.','衣物完全干燥与被雨淋透矛盾。','context'),[Q(1,'How were they after waiting in the rain?','completely wet','warm and dry','covered in dry snow only','Soaked means thoroughly wet.'),Q(1,'Which item is soaked?','a towel saturated with water','a dry towel sealed in a cupboard','a clean, empty jar','The adjective describes something penetrated by liquid.'),Q(1,'What is the base verb of soaked?','soak','sneak','soar','Soaked is the past participle/adjective from soak.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','soaked to the skin','soaked in silence to the floor','soaked a room yesterday','The phrase commonly means completely drenched.')]);
P('soap','Soap comes from Old English sāpe, through Germanic forms from Latin sapo, ultimately borrowed from a Germanic source; it names a washing substance, a TV serial, or the act of rubbing soap on something.',[C('soap.s1','hygiene','Use soap and running water to wash your hands after handling the soil samples.','处理完土壤样品后，用肥皂和流动水洗手。','Use soap and running water','soap 作名词指与水一起清洁身体或衣物的物质。','The first sense is a substance used with water to wash.','第一义是与水一起洗身体或衣物的物质。'),C('soap.s2','television','My grandmother watches a soap after dinner because she enjoys its continuing family story.','祖母晚饭后看一部肥皂剧，因为她喜欢连续展开的家庭故事。','watches a soap','口语名词 soap 可指 soap opera，即讲述一群人日常生活的连续剧。','The second sense is a television serial about a group’s daily lives.','第二义是讲述一群人日常生活的电视连续剧。'),C('soap.s3','cleaning','Soap the stained cloth gently before rinsing it in cool water.','先轻轻给有污渍的布抹上肥皂，再用凉水冲洗。','Soap the stained cloth','soap 作及物动词表示把肥皂擦抹在某物上。','The verb means rub soap on something.','动词义是把肥皂抹在某物上。')],M('She washed her hands with soap by using a dry stone and no washing substance.','She washed her hands with soap by rubbing the washing substance into the skin with water.','干石头并非 soap，洗涤用语不适用于它。','word-choice'),[Q(1,'What should be used to wash hands?','a washing substance with water','a snowdrift','a sports board','Soap is the cleansing substance in the first sense.'),Q(2,'Why does the grandmother watch a soap?','it follows the lives of a group over time','it teaches how to make washing bars only','it is a sports broadcast','A soap is short for a television soap opera.'),Q(3,'What should be done to the stained cloth?','rub soap onto it before rinsing','snare it in wire','soar it above the water','The verb soap means apply soap to a surface.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses soap as a noun for a product?','The soap removed the soil from my hands.','Soap the cloth before washing it.','The show is a soap.','The first is the physical washing substance.')]);
P('soar','Soar came through Anglo-French/Old French essorer, “fly high”; its deeper path is uncertain. The verb covers flying high, rising rapidly, or standing very high.',[C('soar.s1','flight','A red kite soared above the marsh while the wind carried it toward the coast.','风筝被风带向海岸时，一只红色鸢在沼泽上空高高翱翔。','soared above the marsh','soar 的飞行义表示在空中高高飞行。','The first sense is fly high in the air.','第一义是在空中高飞。'),C('soar.s2','prices','Heating costs soared during the coldest month, forcing several families to seek help.','最冷的月份里取暖费用猛涨，迫使几户人家寻求帮助。','costs soared','抽象数值作主语时 soar 表示迅速升至很高水平。','The second sense is rise very quickly to a high level.','第二义是迅速升至很高水平。'),C('soar.s3','landscape','Dark cliffs soar above the beach, casting a long shadow over the path.','深色悬崖高耸于海滩之上，在小路上投下长长的影子。','cliffs soar above','主语为建筑或地形时 soar 可表示高高耸立。','The third sense means be very high or tall.','第三义是高耸。')],M('Heating costs soared during the cold month by falling to their lowest level in years.','Heating costs soared during the cold month by rising sharply to a high level.','降至最低点是下降，不是 soar 所表示的猛增。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Where did the kite fly?','high above the marsh','below the waterline','inside a snowdrift','Soar in the first sense is fly high.'),Q(2,'What happened to heating costs?','they rose quickly to a high level','they fell to a record low','they were used to wash hands','Soar can describe a rapid rise in a figure.'),Q(3,'How did the cliffs look?','very high above the beach','low and hidden under sand','like a snowflake','The third sense means stand very high.'),Q(2,'Which statement is true of soaring prices?','they increase rapidly','they drop sharply','they remain exactly unchanged','The abstract use of soar means rise quickly.')]);
P('soaring','Soaring is soar + -ing, used adjectivally for a bird, structure, price, or figure moving rapidly upward.',C('soaring.s1','cost of living','Soaring rents pushed service workers farther from the city centre, even though their wages stayed flat.','租金飞涨把服务业员工挤得离市中心越来越远，尽管他们的工资没有上涨。','Soaring rents','soaring 作前置形容词，表示数额迅速上升。','Soaring describes something going upward quickly, including prices or figures.','soaring 可形容鸟、建筑、价格或数字快速向上。'),M('The report calls rents soaring because they fell by half and stayed at a record low.','The report calls rents soaring because they rose quickly to a high level.','下降并处于低位不符合 soaring 的上升含义。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What happened to rents?','they rose quickly','they fell by half','they stayed unchanged','Soaring describes rapid upward movement.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is a natural use of soaring?','soaring food prices','soaring warm soap','soaring the rent softly','The adjective modifies prices that are rising fast.'),Q(1,'What happened to wages in the example?','they stayed flat while rents climbed','they soared at the same rate','they became snowboards','The example contrasts rising rents with unchanged wages.'),Q(1,'Soaring can describe…','a figure or object moving rapidly upward','only a person taking a short nap','a small piece cut off with scissors','The adjective extends the verb’s upward movement sense.')]);
})();

(function(){
'use strict';
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const Q=(s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType='meaning')=>({s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:`Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/${w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')}`});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistake,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(contexts)?contexts:[contexts],mistakes:[mistake],quiz:qs.map((q,i)=>({id:w+'.q'+(i+1),senseId:w+'.s'+q.s,prompt:q.prompt,answer:q.answer,options:[q.answer,q.wrong1,q.wrong2],explain:q.explain,errorType:q.errorType,type:'辨义与用法'}))});
P('sob','Sob is an imitative word recorded in Middle English; it echoes the short, broken breaths made while crying.',[C('sob.s1','emotion','The exhausted child sobbed in the hallway until her father knelt down to comfort her.','筋疲力尽的孩子在走廊里抽泣，直到父亲蹲下来安慰她。','sobbed in the hallway','动词指哭泣时短促吸气。','To sob is to cry while taking short, sudden breaths.','sob 指一边哭一边短促地吸气。'),C('sob.s2','sound','A single sob escaped him when he heard that the old dog had been found.','听说那只老狗被找到了，他忍不住发出一声啜泣。','A single sob escaped','可数名词表示一次啜泣或相应声音。','A sob is one act or sound of sobbing.','名词 sob 指一次啜泣或其声音。')],M('The child sobbed by laughing steadily and breathing calmly without any crying.','The child sobbed by crying with short, broken breaths.','平静大笑没有哭泣和急促抽气，不符合 sob。','meaning'),[Q(1,'How was the child crying?','with short, broken breaths','with a steady laugh and no tears','by quietly taking a nap','Sob describes crying with sudden short breaths.'),Q(2,'What escaped him?','one sound of crying','a snowflake','a rubber-soled shoe','A sob as a noun is one act or sound.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses sob as a verb?','She sobbed when she heard the news.','A sob broke the silence.','The sob lasted one second.','The first sentence uses the action verb.'),Q(2,'What does “a sob escaped him” mean?','he made one involuntary crying sound','he sneezed loudly','he left the building','The noun names a short sound of sobbing.')]);
P('sober','Sober comes through Old French from Latin sobrius, “not drunk, temperate,” traditionally analysed as se- “without” + ebrius “drunk”; it also means serious/plain or make serious.',[C('sober.s1','alcohol','The driver stayed sober at the reception and took three colleagues home afterward.','这名司机在招待会上保持清醒，随后开车送三位同事回家。','stayed sober','sober 的基本状态义是没有受到酒精影响。','The first sense means not affected by alcohol.','第一义是没有受到酒精影响、未醉。'),C('sober.s2','reporting','The inspector gave a sober account of the flood damage without exaggerating the losses.','检查员严肃而克制地报告洪灾损失，没有夸大情况。','a sober account','sober 在此表示严肃、持重；也可形容颜色素净。','The second sense is serious or plain in colour.','第二义指严肃持重，也可指颜色朴素。'),C('sober.s3','reaction','The sudden recall notice sobered the team and ended their joking about the defect.','突如其来的召回通知让团队严肃起来，不再拿缺陷开玩笑。','sobered the team','sober 作动词表示使人清醒或变得严肃。','The verb means become or make someone serious, or stop being drunk.','动词表示使人清醒、严肃，或不再醉。')],M('The driver was sober at the reception because alcohol had left him visibly drunk and unable to stand.','The driver was not affected by alcohol, so he remained sober at the reception.','明显醉酒与 sober 的未受酒精影响相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why could the driver take colleagues home?','he was not affected by alcohol','he had been drinking heavily','he was asleep','Sober in the first sense means not drunk.'),Q(2,'How was the inspector’s account?','serious and restrained','brightly colored','a short crying sound','The second sense includes a serious, measured tone.'),Q(3,'What did the recall notice do to the team?','made them serious','made them drunk','helped them snowboard','The verb sober can mean make someone serious.'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses sober in the alcohol sense?','a sober driver','a sober assessment','a sober brown suit','Only the first refers to being unaffected by alcohol.')]);
P('sobriquet','Sobriquet is borrowed from French sobriquet, “nickname”; the French word’s deeper origin is uncertain.',C('sobriquet.s1','names','The newspaper used the sobriquet “River City” for the town, a name residents had embraced for decades.','报纸把该镇称作“河城”，这是居民沿用几十年的绰号。','sobriquet “River City”','同位语说明 sobriquet 是广为人知的非正式称呼。','A sobriquet is an informal name given to a person or place and widely recognized.','sobriquet 是广为人知的人或地方的非正式名称。'),M('The newspaper called the town by a sobriquet, meaning its registered legal name printed on every official deed.','The newspaper called the town by a sobriquet, meaning its familiar informal nickname.','sobriquet 是非正式绰号，不是法定注册名称。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What name did the newspaper use?','a familiar nickname for the town','the town’s legal registration number','a weather report','A sobriquet is an informal recognized name.'),Q(1,'Which could be a sobriquet?','“The Windy City” for Chicago','the date on a birth certificate','a street’s measured width','A sobriquet is a nickname for a person or place.'),Q(1,'What language supplied sobriquet to English?','French','Old English only','Japanese','The word was borrowed from French.'),Q(1,'Why is “River City” a sobriquet here?','residents widely use it as an informal name','it is a chemical formula','it is the town’s formal tax code','The example identifies a familiar nickname.')]);
P('soccer','Soccer is an 1880s English formation from “Association” football: assoc. was shortened and the informal -er ending added.',C('soccer.s1','sport','The school’s soccer team practised passing drills before Saturday’s match.','学校足球队在周六比赛前练习了传球。','soccer team practised','soccer 指两队踢圆球、争取射门得分的运动。','Soccer is a team game in which players kick a ball and try to score goals.','soccer 是两队用脚踢球并争取进球的运动。'),M('The soccer team scored by carrying the ball into the goal with their hands throughout the match.','The soccer team scored by kicking the ball into the goal.','soccer 的核心比赛方式是踢球，不是全程用手抱球进门。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What did the team practise?','passing a ball with their feet','throwing a snowball','swinging a racket','Soccer is played by kicking a ball to score goals.'),Q(1,'How did the word soccer form?','from Association football, shortened with an informal -er ending','from the word snow plus board','from Latin for six','The name arose as an informal shortening of Association football.'),Q(1,'What is the aim in soccer?','score goals against the other team','catch an animal in a snare','make a high jump over the net','Players try to score goals by kicking the ball.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','play soccer on Saturday','play a soccer of water','sneeze soccer into a goal','Soccer is the name of the sport.')]);
P('sociability','Sociability is sociable + -ity, with sociable tracing through French to Latin sociabilis, “fit for companionship,” from socius “companion.”',C('sociability.s1','workplace','The role requires sociability as well as technical skill because staff greet visitors throughout the day.','这份工作既需要专业技能，也需要善于交际，因为员工整天都要接待访客。','requires sociability','抽象名词表示乐意并能够愉快地与他人相处的特质。','Sociability is willingness and ability to spend time pleasantly with other people.','sociability 指乐意并能够愉快地与人相处。'),M('The job requires sociability, so applicants must avoid speaking to visitors or colleagues.','The job requires sociability, so applicants should be comfortable talking with visitors and colleagues.','回避交谈与岗位所需的善于交际相矛盾。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why does the job require sociability?','staff regularly interact with visitors','the job involves repairing snowboards','staff work alone without contact','Sociability is the ability and willingness to enjoy interaction.'),Q(1,'Which behavior shows sociability?','chatting comfortably with new colleagues','refusing to speak to anyone','snubbing every visitor','The noun describes ease in spending time with people.'),Q(1,'What does -ity do in sociability?','forms a noun naming a quality','forms a past tense','means without society','The suffix turns sociable into an abstract noun.'),Q(1,'Which is closest to sociability?','a friendly readiness to engage with others','a dislike of all social contact','a field of genetic biology','Sociability names a social quality.')]);
P('sociable','Sociable came through French sociable from Latin sociabilis, “fit for companionship,” from socius “companion”; it describes a friendly person or a setting that encourages interaction.',[C('sociable.s1','personality','At the conference, Jia was sociable and introduced herself to people from several research groups.','会议上，佳很合群，主动向几个研究组的人作了自我介绍。','was sociable and introduced herself','sociable 描写友好且愿意与他人相处的人。','The first sense is friendly and happy to spend time with other people.','第一义指友好且乐意与人交往。'),C('sociable.s2','space','The kitchen is the most sociable room in their flat because everyone gathers there to talk.','厨房是他们公寓里最适合交流的房间，因为大家都聚在那里聊天。','most sociable room','sociable 也描述便于交谈、共处的场所或活动。','The second sense means a setting makes it easy for people to talk together.','第二义指场所便于人们交流共处。')],M('The kitchen was sociable because its layout separated everyone into soundproof rooms where they could not talk.','The kitchen was sociable because its open layout let everyone sit together and talk.','隔音分隔且无法交谈的空间不利于社交。','context'),[Q(1,'How did Jia behave at the conference?','she introduced herself and talked with people','she refused to meet anyone','she inspected a snare','Sociable describes a friendly, outgoing person.'),Q(2,'Why was the kitchen sociable?','people naturally gathered there to talk','it kept everyone in separate soundproof rooms','it was a social science textbook','A sociable space encourages interaction.'),Q(1,'Which person is sociable?','someone who enjoys meeting and talking with others','someone who avoids every conversation','someone who snoops through private files','The first sense describes friendly interaction.'),Q(2,'Which place is sociable in the setting sense?','a shared lounge with seats arranged for conversation','a locked storage closet','a silent examination booth','The second sense applies to places that make interaction easy.')]);
P('sociably','Sociably is sociable + -ly; it describes speaking or behaving in a friendly way that shows readiness to interact.',C('sociably.s1','conversation','The retired neighbours chatted sociably with the new family while they waited for the lift.','退休邻居等电梯时，和新搬来的家庭亲切地聊了起来。','chatted sociably with','副词修饰 chatted，说明交谈友好随和。','Sociably means in a friendly manner, ready to talk with others.','sociably 表示亲切随和地、愿意与人交谈地。'),M('The neighbours chatted sociably by refusing to answer, turning away, and ending every conversation.','The neighbours chatted sociably by responding warmly and keeping the conversation going.','拒绝回应并结束谈话不是友好交谈。','usage'),[Q(1,'How did the neighbours chat?','in a friendly, open manner','in a hostile silence','with a snowstorm','Sociably describes friendly interaction.'),Q(1,'Which action is sociable?','asking a newcomer about their journey and listening','ignoring everyone at a gathering','searching a colleague’s desk','The adverb describes an outgoing conversational manner.'),Q(1,'What word does sociably come from?','sociable','sociology','soccer','Sociably is formed by adding -ly to sociable.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','talk sociably with guests','sociably the room is six','sociably a snowdrift','The adverb modifies a social action such as talking.')]);
P('social','Social comes from Latin socialis, “of companionship or allies,” from socius “companion”; it relates to society, interaction with others, or a gathering.',[C('social.s1','public policy','The report examines social problems caused by unequal access to housing and health care.','报告研究了住房和医疗机会不平等引发的社会问题。','social problems','social 修饰 problems，表示与社会及人们共同生活相关。','The first sense relates to society and how people live together.','第一义是与社会及人们共同生活有关。'),C('social.s2','interaction','Her social life became busier after she joined the neighbourhood choir.','加入社区合唱团后，她的社交生活变得更丰富。','social life','social 可指与朋友聚会、交往有关的活动。','The second sense relates to meeting people and spending time with friends.','第二义与结交朋友、聚会往来有关。'),C('social.s3','event','The club’s monthly social brought members together for conversation and a shared meal.','俱乐部每月举办联谊活动，让会员聚在一起交谈并共进晚餐。','monthly social','名词 social 指人们聚会交谈的非正式活动。','As a noun, a social is an informal party where people meet and talk.','名词义是人们聚会交谈的非正式活动。')],M('The club held a social by cancelling the gathering and asking members not to meet or talk.','The club held a social by bringing members together to talk and share a meal.','取消聚会并禁止交流与 social 活动的目的相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What does social problems describe?','issues connected with how people live together','a particular shoe size','one person’s bedtime','The first sense concerns society.'),Q(2,'What changed after choir membership?','her opportunities to meet friends increased','her health care disappeared','the monthly club gathering ended','Social life concerns interaction with people.'),Q(3,'What was the club’s monthly social?','an informal gathering for members','a policy report','a snowstorm','A social as a noun is a party or gathering.'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses social for society-wide matters?','social inequality','a social at the club','a social life after work','The first phrase relates to social structures.')]);
P('social science','Social science is the compound social + science; it names academic fields that study society, human behaviour, and institutions.',C('social science.s1','education','She moved from physics to social science to study how housing policy affects family health.','她从物理学转到社会科学，研究住房政策如何影响家庭健康。','moved from physics to social science','学科总称，包含研究社会、人类行为与制度的领域。','Social science includes academic subjects such as economics and politics that examine society and behaviour.','social science 是研究社会与行为的学科总称，如经济学和政治学。'),M('She chose social science to study planets, stars, and the chemical composition of distant moons.','She chose social science to study housing policy, institutions, and human behaviour.','天体与行星通常属于自然科学，不是社会科学的研究对象。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What question did she study?','how housing policy affects family health','how stars form in a nebula','how to wax a snowboard','Social science examines society and human behaviour.'),Q(1,'Which subject is a social science?','economics','astrophysics','organic chemistry','Economics studies people, institutions, and social systems.'),Q(1,'What is the scope of social science?','society, behaviour, and institutions','only rocks and chemical elements','only individual sleep habits','The compound names academic study of social life.'),Q(1,'Why is politics a social science?','it studies institutions and collective human decisions','it measures snowflakes','it is a form of football','Social science includes fields examining society and institutions.')]);
P('socialism','Socialism is social + -ism, formed for political doctrines favouring public or collective ownership and greater equality; movements differ in how they pursue those aims.',C('socialism.s1','politics','The seminar compared several forms of socialism and asked how each organizes public ownership and equality.','研讨会比较了几种社会主义形式，并讨论各自如何组织公有制与平等。','forms of socialism','-ism 构成政治思想体系名词；具体流派和制度安排各有差异。','Socialism is a set of political beliefs favouring public ownership and greater equality.','socialism 是主张公有制和更大平等的一套政治信念。'),M('The lecturer defined socialism as a doctrine that rejects any public ownership and opposes greater equality.','The lecturer defined socialism as a family of doctrines that generally favours public or collective ownership and greater equality.','拒绝公有制并反对平等与词条所述核心主张相反。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What political ideas were compared?','views favouring public ownership and greater equality','methods for building snowboards','rules for a soccer match','Those are central themes associated with socialism.'),Q(1,'Why does socialism have -ism?','the ending forms a noun for a doctrine or system of beliefs','it marks a plural of society','it means without social contact','-ism often forms a name for a belief system.'),Q(1,'Which topic belongs in a discussion of socialism?','how services or industries are collectively owned','how a snowflake branches','how to detect gas with a sniffer','Socialism concerns political organization and ownership.'),Q(1,'What caution does the example include?','different movements arrange ownership and equality differently','all forms are identical in every detail','socialism is simply a social party','The term covers a range of political approaches.')]);
P('socialization','Socialization is socialize + -ation; it names the process through which people, especially children, learn group norms and ways of living together.',C('socialization.s1','development','School clubs and playground games contribute to children’s socialization by teaching them to share rules and take turns.','学校社团和操场游戏通过教孩子遵守规则、轮流参与，促进他们的社会化。','children’s socialization','socialization 指学习群体生活方式和规范的过程。','It is the process by which people learn to live in a group.','socialization 是人们学习群体生活的过程。'),M('The programme supported children’s socialization by keeping them isolated from all groups and preventing interaction.','The programme supported children’s socialization by giving them guided chances to interact with groups.','与所有群体隔离会阻碍学习群体互动规范。','context'),[Q(1,'What do children learn through socialization?','group norms such as sharing and taking turns','how to remain permanently isolated','how to measure rainfall','Socialization is learning to live in a group.'),Q(1,'Which experience can aid socialization?','a club where children cooperate under shared rules','a room where no one can interact','a private list of snowdrifts','Group activities teach interaction and norms.'),Q(1,'What does -ation contribute to socialization?','a noun for a process','a past-tense verb ending','a person who studies sociology','The suffix forms an action/process noun.'),Q(1,'Who is especially learning during early socialization?','children learning how to participate in a community','a snowflake melting','a lone animal in a trap','The source sense highlights learning group life.')]);
P('socialize','Socialize combines social + -ize, the verb-forming suffix “make or become”; it means spend time with others, network for work, or help a group become integrated.',[C('socialize.s1','leisure','Guests socialized in the garden before dinner, sharing stories while the children played nearby.','晚餐前，客人们在花园里交谈交往，孩子们在旁边玩耍。','Guests socialized in the garden','不及物用法指轻松友好地与人交往。','The first sense is spend relaxed, friendly time with other people.','第一义是轻松友好地与他人相处。'),C('socialize.s2','career','At the conference, he socialized with editors who might commission his next book.','会上，他结识并交谈了可能委托他写下一本书的编辑。','socialized with editors','此处表示为事业或生意结识可能有帮助的人。','The second sense is meet people who may be useful for career or business.','第二义是为事业或生意拓展人脉。'),C('socialize.s3','integration','The orientation course helps international students socialize with classmates through shared projects.','迎新课程通过合作项目帮助国际学生与同学打成一片。','helps ... socialize with classmates','help + object + bare infinitive；此处是融入群体活动。','The third sense is spend time with a group and take part in its activities.','第三义是与群体共处并参与其活动。')],M('He socialized with the editors by avoiding every conversation and leaving before meeting anyone.','He socialized with the editors by introducing himself and discussing possible projects.','回避交谈、未与任何人见面不符合 socialize。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the guests do before dinner?','spent relaxed time talking with one another','studied social science exams','snubbed every visitor','Socialize can mean mingle in a friendly way.'),Q(2,'Why did he talk with the editors?','to build professional contacts for future work','to avoid all career connections','to learn how to snowboard','This use means network with people who may help a career.'),Q(3,'How does the orientation course help students?','it lets them join shared projects and get to know classmates','it keeps them apart from the class','it teaches them to play soccer only','The third sense is becoming part of a group.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses socialize for casual interaction?','We socialized over coffee after the lecture.','She socialized her colleagues for a new project.','He socialized a set of numbers.','The first phrase describes relaxed conversation.')]);
P('socially','Socially is social + -ly; it means with regard to society, class, or interaction with other people.',C('socially.s1','public impact','The policy is economically efficient but socially costly because low-income tenants lose access to nearby services.','这项政策经济上有效率，却在社会层面代价高昂，因为低收入租户失去了附近服务。','socially costly','副词修饰 costly，表示从社会影响角度来看代价大。','Socially concerns society, class, or interaction with other people.','socially 指在社会、阶层或人际交往层面。'),M('The policy was socially costly because it improved access for every low-income tenant and caused no loss of services.','The policy was socially costly because low-income tenants lost access to nearby services.','改善所有人服务可及性与文中所述社会代价相反。','context'),[Q(1,'Why was the policy socially costly?','low-income tenants lost nearby services','it reduced the price of a snowflake','it improved every tenant’s access','Socially relates the cost to society and affected groups.'),Q(1,'Which question is social rather than purely personal?','How does the rule affect different communities?','What is the exact colour of my cup?','How many centimetres is a snowboard?','The adverb concerns wider social effects.'),Q(1,'What does -ly do in socially?','forms an adverb from social','forms the plural of society','turns the word into a noun','The suffix creates an adverb.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is correct?','socially responsible policy','socially a policy of six','socially the snow melted','The adverb modifies a judgement about a policy.')]);
P('society','Society comes through French société from Latin societas, “fellowship, association,” from socius “companion”; it can mean people collectively, an association, or the fashionable upper class.',[C('society.s1','community','Technology is changing society by altering how people work, communicate, and share information.','技术正在改变社会，影响人们工作、沟通和分享信息的方式。','changing society','society 作集合名词指共同生活、有共享法律和习俗的人群。','The first sense is people in general living together with shared laws and customs.','第一义是共同生活并有共享法律和习俗的人们。'),C('society.s2','organization','She joined the local astronomy society to attend lectures and observe the night sky with other members.','她加入了当地天文学会，以便参加讲座并与其他成员一起观测夜空。','astronomy society','society 可指有共同兴趣的组织或协会。','The second sense is an organization of people with a shared interest.','第二义是有共同兴趣的人组成的组织。'),C('society.s3','class','The novel describes high society as a small circle of wealthy families who control the season’s invitations.','小说把上流社会描写成一小群富有家族，他们掌控着当季的邀请名单。','high society','high society 是指富有、时髦的社会群体。','The third sense is the rich and fashionable group of people.','第三义是富有而时髦的人群。')],M('The local astronomy society was a snowstorm because it consisted of falling ice crystals, not people with a shared interest.','The local astronomy society was an organization of people with a shared interest in astronomy.','冰晶天气现象不是由共同兴趣成员组成的协会。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What is changing in the technology example?','people’s shared ways of living and communicating','the astronomy club’s membership list only','a single person’s shoe size','Society as a whole is the collective population and its life.'),Q(2,'Why did she join the astronomy society?','to meet others who share an interest','to become a member of the upper class','to collect snowdrifts','The organization sense groups people around a shared interest.'),Q(3,'Who makes up high society in the novel?','wealthy and fashionable families','all people under a particular law','members of a local astronomy club','The third sense is the elite social class.'),Q(2,'Which use means an association?','a society for local historians','society is changing quickly','high society attended the gala','The first phrase is a shared-interest organization.')]);
P('sociobiology','Sociobiology combines socio- (from Latin socius, “companion”) + biology; it studies social behaviour through evolution and genetics.',C('sociobiology.s1','science','The lecture introduced sociobiology by examining how kinship and natural selection may shape animal cooperation.','讲座通过考察亲缘关系和自然选择如何影响动物合作，介绍了社会生物学。','introduced sociobiology by examining','学科名指用自然选择与遗传解释社会行为的研究领域。','Sociobiology explains social behaviour through natural selection and genetics.','sociobiology 用自然选择和遗传解释社会行为。'),M('The lecture called a study of planetary rock chemistry sociobiology even though it examined no organisms or social behaviour.','The lecture called a study of animal cooperation and genetic influences sociobiology.','行星岩石化学不研究生物社会行为。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What did the lecture examine?','how kinship and selection may shape cooperation','how to polish a snowboard','how to organize a soccer league only','Sociobiology studies social behavior using evolution and genetics.'),Q(1,'Which topic fits sociobiology?','possible genetic influences on group behaviour','the chemical composition of a distant moon','the history of a nickname','The field combines biological and social explanations.'),Q(1,'What does socio- relate to?','companionship or social life','snowfall','a unit of sixty','The prefix comes from Latin socius, companion.'),Q(1,'Why can applying sociobiology to human morals be controversial?','explaining behaviour biologically can raise disputed claims','the word means a social gathering','it is a sport played on snow','The field’s application to human behavior can be debated.')]);
P('sociologist','Sociologist is sociology + -ist, naming a scholar who studies social groups, institutions, and behaviour.',C('sociologist.s1','research','A sociologist interviewed tenants in the new development to learn how the layout affected neighbourly contact.','一位社会学家采访了新开发区的租户，以了解布局如何影响邻里交往。','A sociologist interviewed tenants','sociologist 指研究社会群体、制度和行为的学者。','A sociologist studies social groups, institutions, and behaviour.','sociologist 是研究社会群体、制度与行为的学者。'),M('The sociologist interviewed tenants about social groups, but the article says she was a professional snowboard racer.','The sociologist interviewed tenants about social groups as part of her research.','职业单板运动员的身份不等于研究社会群体的学者。','word-choice'),[Q(1,'What was the researcher studying?','how building layout affected neighbours','how to detect gas leaks','how to score goals in soccer','A sociologist examines social interaction and institutions.'),Q(1,'Who is a sociologist?','a scholar studying society and social behaviour','a person who only designs snowboards','a member of every social club by definition','The occupation is an academic study of social life.'),Q(1,'How is sociologist formed?','sociology + -ist','snow + board + -er','sociable + -ly','The suffix -ist names a person in a field.'),Q(1,'Which source would a sociologist likely interview?','families in a new housing development','a snowflake under a microscope only','a piece of soap','The example concerns people and communities.')]);
P('sociology','Sociology was coined in the 19th century from Latin socius “companion” + Greek -logia “study”; it is the academic study of society and social groups.',C('sociology.s1','education','In sociology, the class compared how two neighbourhoods organize childcare and public transport.','社会学课上，学生比较了两个社区如何组织托育和公共交通。','In sociology','学科名指研究社会、社会群体及其行为。','Sociology is the academic study of society, social groups, and their behaviour.','sociology 是研究社会、社会群体及其行为的学科。'),M('The sociology project studied only the chemical bonds in soap, with no people, groups, or institutions involved.','The sociology project studied how neighbourhood groups organized childcare and transport.','单纯研究肥皂化学键不属于研究社会群体与行为。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What did the class compare?','how neighbourhoods organize services','how snowflakes melt','how a snare catches a rabbit','Sociology examines people and social arrangements.'),Q(1,'Which question belongs to sociology?','How do schools shape community relationships?','What is the atomic number of sodium?','How fast can a snowboard descend?','Sociology studies society and behaviour.'),Q(1,'What roots appear in the word’s formation?','Latin socius and Greek -logia','Old English snaw and board','French soap and -er','The name combines a social root with “study.”'),Q(1,'What does sociology study?','society, groups, and their behaviour','only individual weather reports','the structure of a window socket','The academic discipline is about social life.')]);
P('sock','Sock comes from Old English socc, from Latin soccus, a light shoe; the verb “hit hard” is a separate later colloquial use of uncertain origin.',[C('sock.s1','clothing','She put on a clean pair of wool socks before walking across the cold tile floor.','她穿上一双干净的羊毛短袜，才走过冰冷的瓷砖地面。','a pair of wool socks','名词指覆盖脚和小腿下部的柔软衣物。','A sock covers the foot and lower leg.','sock 是覆盖脚和小腿下部的柔软衣物。'),C('sock.s2','colloquial','In the old comedy, the hero socked the bully on the jaw after he shoved a friend.','在那部老喜剧里，英雄在恶霸推搡朋友后猛击了他的下巴。','socked the bully on the jaw','口语动词 sock someone 表示用力打某人。','The colloquial verb means hit someone hard.','口语动词义是用力打某人。')],M('She wore a sock on her foot, but the sentence describes it as a hard punch delivered to a bully.','She wore a sock on her foot, a soft garment covering the foot and lower leg.','穿在脚上的衣物是名词义，不是口语动词“猛击”。','word-choice'),[Q(1,'What did she put on her foot?','a soft garment covering the foot and lower leg','a wall electrical outlet','a baseball','Sock as a noun is an item of clothing.'),Q(2,'What did the hero do to the bully?','hit him hard on the jaw','put a wool garment on his foot','invite him to a social','The informal verb sock means strike forcefully.'),Q(1,'Which use is the clothing noun?','a pair of dry socks','he socked the bully','sock the opponent hard','The first phrase names garments.'),Q(2,'What does “socked him on the jaw” mean?','punched him hard','gave him a clean sock','sniffed at him','The verb describes a strong hit.')]);
P('socket','Socket came through French socquet, a small socket; the deeper source is uncertain. It names an electrical outlet or a hollow joint into which another part fits.',[C('socket.s1','electricity','Unplug the lamp from the wall socket before replacing its damaged cord.','更换损坏的电线前，先把台灯从墙上插座拔下。','wall socket','socket 指墙上供插头插入的电源装置。','The first sense is a wall device into which an electric plug fits.','第一义是墙上供电源插头插入的装置。'),C('socket.s2','anatomy','The head of the thigh bone fits into a socket in the pelvis, forming the hip joint.','股骨头嵌入骨盆的关节窝，形成髋关节。','fits into a socket','socket 也指另一部件嵌入的中空凹处。','The second sense is a hollow part into which another part fits.','第二义是供另一部分嵌入的凹窝。')],M('The thigh bone fits into a socket, which the anatomy note defines as a solid ridge with no hollow space.','The thigh bone fits into a socket, a hollow joint space in the pelvis.','socket 在关节义中是容纳骨头的凹窝，不是实心凸脊。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Where should the lamp be unplugged?','from the wall outlet','from the hip joint','from a snowdrift','A wall socket accepts an electrical plug.'),Q(2,'What does the thigh bone fit into?','a hollow joint space in the pelvis','a wall plug','a wool sock','The anatomical sense is a hollow part for another part.'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses socket for electricity?','plug it into the socket','the bone fits into its socket','a socket of snow fell','The first phrase is an electrical outlet.'),Q(2,'What do both senses have in common?','one part fits into a hollow opening','both are soft clothing','both mean a social group','A socket is a receptacle or hollow fitting.')]);
P('sod','Sod is Old English sod, related to Dutch zode, for a piece of turf with its soil and roots; it is commonly cut and laid as grass.',C('sod.s1','landscaping','Workers laid fresh sod along the path so the bare ground would become a lawn.','工人沿着小路铺上新草皮，让裸露地面变成草坪。','laid fresh sod','sod 指连草和根一起切下、可铺设的一块草皮和土。','A sod is a section of soil with grass and roots cut for laying as turf.','sod 是连根切下、用来铺草坪的一块草和土。'),M('The landscapers laid sod, which the plan defines as bare concrete with no grass or soil.','The landscapers laid sod, sections of grass with roots and soil, over the bare ground.','没有草和土的混凝土不属于 sod。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did workers lay beside the path?','a section of grass with soil and roots','a wire loop','a socket for a plug','Sod is turf cut with its roots and soil.'),Q(1,'Why did they lay sod?','to cover bare ground with a lawn','to create an electrical outlet','to build a snowdrift','Sod can be placed to establish grass.'),Q(1,'Which material is sod?','a cut square of turf including soil','a sheet of plastic grass with no soil','a snowflake crystal','The source sense includes grass and roots with soil.'),Q(1,'What is a natural verb with sod?','lay sod along the path','sod a soccer ball with soap','sod the socket to size','Sod is commonly laid as turf.')]);
})();

(function(){
'use strict';
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const Q=(s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType='meaning')=>({s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:`Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/${w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')}`});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistake,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(contexts)?contexts:[contexts],mistakes:[mistake],quiz:qs.map((q,i)=>({id:w+'.q'+(i+1),senseId:w+'.s'+q.s,prompt:q.prompt,answer:q.answer,options:[q.answer,q.wrong1,q.wrong2],explain:q.explain,errorType:q.errorType,type:'辨义与用法'}))});
P('soda','Soda entered English through Italian soda; its deeper origin is uncertain. The word later named soda ash and drinks made bubbly with dissolved gas.',[C('soda.s1','drinks','At the diner, Lee ordered a lemon soda with ice while his friend chose still water.','在小餐馆里，李点了一杯加冰柠檬汽水，朋友则选了普通水。','lemon soda with ice','soda 可指带气饮料，也可指加气的水。','The first sense is a sweet fizzy drink or water with gas added.','第一义是含糖汽水或加了气的水。'),C('soda.s2','cooking','The recipe calls for baking soda, not washing soda, to help the cake rise.','食谱要求用小苏打而不是洗涤碱，让蛋糕发起来。','baking soda, not washing soda','第二义指用于清洁和某些食品的苏打类白色粉末。','The second sense is a white chemical powder used in cleaning or some foods.','第二义是用于清洁或食品的白色苏打粉末。')],M('The baker added soda to the cake, meaning a bottle of fizzy lemon drink rather than a measured powder.','The baker added baking soda, the white powder used to help the cake rise.','此处烘焙配方需要的是粉末，不是汽水饮料。','word-choice'),[Q(1,'What did Lee order?','a sweet fizzy drink','a cleaning powder','a metal element','Soda in the diner context is a bubbly drink.'),Q(2,'Which ingredient helps the cake rise?','baking soda powder','a bottle of lemon soda','a snowflake','The recipe uses the chemical powder, not the beverage.'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses soda as a beverage?','a cherry soda with ice','a spoonful of baking soda','soda ash for cleaning','The drink sense covers sweet fizzy drinks.'),Q(2,'What does baking soda name here?','a white powder used in food','a fizzy water with gas','a soft seating item','The second sense is the chemical powder.')]);
P('sodium','Sodium was coined in 1807 by Humphry Davy from soda + the element-name ending -ium; it names the soft silvery metal Na found in compounds such as table salt.',C('sodium.s1','chemistry','The nutrition label lists sodium, the element present in ordinary table salt as part of sodium chloride.','营养标签列出了钠，它是普通食盐中氯化钠的一种元素。','lists sodium','sodium 是化学元素，符号 Na，存在于盐中。','Sodium is a soft silver metal with the chemical symbol Na.','sodium 是一种柔软银白色金属，化学符号为 Na。'),M('The sample contained sodium, whose chemical symbol is Na, but the lab report labels it as Si.','The sample contained sodium (Na), while Si is the symbol for silicon.','钠的符号是 Na；Si 表示硅。','confusable'),[Q(1,'What is the chemical symbol for sodium?','Na','Si','Sn','Sodium’s symbol is Na.'),Q(1,'Where is sodium found in common table salt?','as part of sodium chloride','as pure liquid metal in a salt shaker','as the element carbon','Table salt contains sodium combined with chlorine.'),Q(1,'What kind of element is sodium?','a soft, silvery metal','a gaseous noble element','a type of soap','The source defines sodium as a soft silver metal.'),Q(1,'How was the name sodium formed?','from soda plus the element ending -ium','from snow plus -board','from Latin for companion','Davy coined the name from soda with -ium.')]);
P('sofa','Sofa came through European languages from Arabic ṣuffa, a raised bench or platform; it names a long upholstered seat for more than one person.',C('sofa.s1','furniture','Three guests sat on the sofa after dinner, with enough room for everyone to lean back.','晚餐后，三位客人坐在沙发上，每个人都有足够空间靠着休息。','sat on the sofa','名词指有靠背和扶手、可供多人坐的长软座。','A sofa is a long comfortable seat with a back and arms for several people.','sofa 是有靠背和扶手、可供多人坐的长软座。'),M('Three guests sat on the sofa, a single narrow stool with no back or arms.','Three guests sat on the sofa, a long padded seat with a back and arms.','单人窄凳不是可供多人坐的沙发。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Where did the guests sit?','on a long comfortable seat for several people','on a wall socket','on a snowdrift','A sofa seats more than one person and has a back and arms.'),Q(1,'Which object is a sofa?','a padded three-seat couch with arms','a single backless stool','a kitchen electrical outlet','The source definition describes a long seat with back and arms.'),Q(1,'How did sofa reach English?','through European languages from Arabic ṣuffa','from Latin for sodium','from Old English for snow','Its history traces to an Arabic word for a bench.'),Q(1,'Which verb naturally goes with sofa in this example?','sit on','sneeze through','snipe at','People sit on a sofa.')]);
P('soft','Soft is Old English sōfte, “gently, easily,” related to a Germanic word for smooth or mild; it describes yielding texture, gentle sound/light, or lenient character.',[C('soft.s1','texture','The mattress felt too soft, so her back sank lower than it did on the firm guest bed.','床垫太软了，她的背陷得比睡在硬实的客床上更深。','mattress felt too soft','触感义表示不硬、容易按压。','The first sense is not hard or firm and easy to press.','第一义是不硬、容易按下去。'),C('soft.s2','sound','The guide spoke in a soft voice so the sleeping birds would not be disturbed.','向导轻声说话，以免惊扰正在休息的鸟。','in a soft voice','soft 可表示声音不大、柔和；也可形容柔和的光或不强烈的程度。','The second sense is not loud, bright, or strong.','第二义表示声音不大、光线不刺眼或强度不高。'),C('soft.s3','strictness','The judge was not soft on repeat offenders and imposed the full penalty allowed by law.','法官对屡犯者并不手软，判处了法律允许的全部刑罚。','not soft on repeat offenders','soft on someone 表示宽容、不够严格。','The third sense means kind or not strict enough.','第三义指心软、宽容或不够严厉。')],M('The judge was soft on repeat offenders because he imposed the harshest penalty and refused to show leniency.','The judge was not soft on repeat offenders because he imposed the full penalty.','不宽容且判重罚，与 soft 表示心软、不够严厉相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did her back sink into the mattress?','it was yielding and easy to press','it was unusually firm','it was made of silver','Soft in sense 1 describes a surface that is not hard.'),Q(2,'Why did the guide use a soft voice?','to keep the sound gentle and quiet','to make the light less bright','to make the bed less firm','The second sense concerns low volume.'),Q(3,'What does “not soft on repeat offenders” mean?','not lenient or insufficiently strict','very gentle in texture','quietly spoken','Soft on someone is about leniency.'),Q(2,'Which is soft light?','a gentle, low-intensity glow','a loud alarm','a strict court ruling','Soft can describe subdued light or sound.')]);
P('soft drink','Soft drink combines soft + drink; soft distinguishes a non-alcoholic beverage from an alcoholic “hard” drink.',C('soft drink.s1','beverages','They ordered a soft drink for the driver and a bottle of water for the passenger.','他们给司机点了无酒精饮料，给乘客点了一瓶水。','ordered a soft drink','soft drink 指上桌时不含酒精的冷饮，常带气或含糖。','A soft drink is a cold sweet or fizzy drink served without alcohol.','soft drink 是不含酒精的冷饮，常含糖或带气。'),M('The waiter brought a soft drink, which contained vodka and was served as an alcoholic cocktail.','The waiter brought a soft drink, a non-alcoholic cold beverage.','含伏特加的鸡尾酒是含酒精饮料，不属于 soft drink。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What did the driver receive?','a cold non-alcoholic drink','an alcoholic cocktail','a bottle of motor oil','A soft drink is served without alcohol.'),Q(1,'Which is a soft drink?','sparkling lemonade','a glass of wine','a shot of vodka','The term distinguishes non-alcoholic beverages.'),Q(1,'Why might a driver choose a soft drink?','it contains no alcohol','it is always served hot','it is a type of softcover book','Soft here contrasts with alcoholic drinks.'),Q(1,'What does soft indicate in soft drink?','non-alcoholic','low in temperature only','made from softwood','The compound names a beverage without alcohol.')]);
P('softball','Softball is named from the larger ball used in the game, originally softer than a baseball; it is a team bat-and-ball sport with underarm pitching.',C('softball.s1','sport','The university softball team practised underarm pitches with a larger ball before the tournament.','大学垒球队在比赛前用较大的球练习了下手投球。','softball team practised underarm pitches','名词指类似棒球的团体击球运动，球较大且下手投球。','Softball is a team bat-and-ball game with a larger ball pitched underarm.','softball 是使用较大球、下手投球的团体击球运动。'),M('The softball match used a tiny golf ball pitched overhand at each batter.','The softball match used a larger ball pitched underarm to each batter.','小高尔夫球和上手投球不符合垒球规则特征。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What kind of pitch did they practise?','underarm pitches with a larger ball','overhand pitches with a tiny golf ball','a soccer kick','The sport typically uses a larger ball pitched underarm.'),Q(1,'What equipment is central to softball?','a bat and a ball','a snowboard and bindings','a wall socket','Softball is a team bat-and-ball game.'),Q(1,'Why is “soft” in softball?','the name refers historically to the ball used, not a ball that is always soft','players must use a soft pillow','the sport is played on snow','The name arose from the ball’s earlier characteristics.'),Q(1,'Which statement best distinguishes softball from soccer?','softball uses a bat and underarm pitch','soccer uses bats to hit a ball','softball is a kind of snowstorm','The game is a bat-and-ball sport.')]);
P('softcover','Softcover combines soft + cover and contrasts with hardcover; as a noun it is a flexible-card-covered book, and as an adjective it describes that kind of book.',[C('softcover.s1','publishing','The library bought a softcover of the novel because its flexible card cover cost less than the hardback.','图书馆买了这本小说的平装本，因为软纸板封面比精装本便宜。','bought a softcover','名词指用薄而有弹性的纸板作封面的书。','A softcover is a book with a flexible card cover rather than stiff board.','softcover 是封面由柔软纸板而非厚硬纸板制成的书。'),C('softcover.s2','publishing','She chose the softcover edition for her backpack because it bent easily without a heavy board cover.','她为背包选了平装版，因为它容易弯折，没有沉重硬封面。','softcover edition','作定语或形容词时描述书籍封面材料柔软。','The adjective means having a thin flexible-card cover.','形容词义是封面为薄而有弹性的软纸板。')],M('The softcover edition had a thick rigid board cover that could not bend.','The softcover edition had a thin flexible card cover.','厚硬不可弯的纸板封面是 hardcover，不是 softcover。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Why did the library buy the softcover?','its flexible card cover cost less','it had a heavy rigid board cover','it was a software program','The noun names a flexible-covered book.'),Q(2,'What made her edition useful in a backpack?','its cover was light and flexible','it was bound in thick wood','it was a social science degree','The adjective describes the flexible cover.'),Q(1,'Which book is a softcover?','a paperback with a bendable card cover','a hardback with rigid boards','an audiobook with no physical cover','Softcover contrasts with stiff hardcover.'),Q(2,'How is softcover used in “softcover edition”?','as an adjective describing the cover type','as a verb meaning to soften','as a noun for furniture','It modifies edition by describing its binding.')]);
P('soften','Soften is soft + -en, a verb meaning make or become less hard, less severe, gentler in manner, or less firm through warmth.',[C('soften.s1','texture','Warm water softened the dried paint enough for the scraper to remove it from the jar.','温水把干硬的颜料泡软了，刮刀得以将它从罐子里刮下。','Warm water softened','及物用法使某物变软、不再那么硬。','The first sense means make something less hard to touch.','第一义是使某物不那么硬、变软。'),C('soften.s2','severity','The company softened its return policy by extending the deadline from seven to thirty days.','公司把退货期限从七天延长到三十天，从而缓和了退货政策。','softened its return policy','比喻义表示减轻严厉程度、让规则没那么苛刻。','The second sense makes something less harsh or severe.','第二义是使某事不那么严厉或严重。'),C('soften.s3','speech','When the child began to cry, the coach softened her voice and knelt beside him.','孩子哭起来时，教练放柔了声音，跪在他身边。','softened her voice','soften 可使说话声或语气更温和、更轻。','The third sense makes a voice or manner gentler and quieter.','第三义是使声音或方式更温和轻柔。'),C('soften.s4','temperature','Leave the butter on the counter for twenty minutes and it will soften without melting.','把黄油放在台面上二十分钟，它会变软但不会融化。','butter ... will soften','不及物用法可指因温度升高而变软或失去硬度。','The fourth sense is become soft or liquid because of warmth.','第四义是受热后变软，或逐渐失去硬度。')],M('The warm water softened the dried paint by making it harder and more brittle.','The warm water softened the dried paint by making it less hard and easier to scrape.','变硬变脆与 soften“变软”相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did warm water do to the paint?','made it less hard and easier to scrape','made it more brittle','turned it into a snowstorm','The first sense is make something softer.'),Q(2,'How did the policy change?','it became less strict by extending the deadline','it became harsher and shorter','it was covered in paint','The second sense reduces severity.'),Q(3,'What changed in the coach’s voice?','it became gentler and quieter','it became more threatening','it turned into a melody','The third sense concerns a gentler manner or voice.'),Q(4,'What happens to butter on the counter?','it becomes less firm as it warms','it freezes into a solid block','it becomes a social drink','The intransitive sense is lose firmness with warmth.')]);
P('softener','Softener is soften + -er, an agent/instrument noun for a chemical or appliance that reduces hardness in water or fabric.',C('softener.s1','laundry','She added fabric softener to the final rinse so the towels would not feel stiff.','她在最后一次漂洗时加入衣物柔顺剂，这样毛巾就不会发硬。','added fabric softener','softener 指减少水或衣物硬度的化学品或设备。','A softener is a chemical or appliance that reduces hardness.','softener 是降低硬度的化学品或器具。'),M('She added fabric softener to make the towels stiff and scratchy after washing.','She added fabric softener so the towels would feel softer after washing.','柔顺剂用来减轻僵硬感，不是让毛巾更刺硬。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did she add fabric softener?','to reduce stiffness in the towels','to make them more scratchy','to colour them silver','A softener makes fabric less stiff.'),Q(1,'Which object can be a softener?','a water-treatment device that reduces hardness','a snowflake detector','a rigid board cover','The noun includes appliances as well as chemicals.'),Q(1,'What does -er contribute in softener?','an agent or instrument that softens','a plural noun ending','a verb meaning to become soft','The suffix forms an instrument/agent noun.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a water softener','a softener the towel quickly','a softener of six','A water softener reduces water hardness.')]);
P('softie','Softie is soft + -ie, an informal noun for someone who is easily moved by others’ feelings and finds it hard to refuse them.',C('softie.s1','personality','He is a softie with the puppies and always agrees to foster one more when the shelter calls.','他对小狗心软，收容所每次来电话，他都答应再寄养一只。','a softie with the puppies','softie 是口语名词，指容易同情人、难以拒绝的人。','A softie feels sorry for others easily and finds it hard to say no.','softie 指容易同情别人、很难拒绝的人。'),M('She is a softie with the children because she never listens to their feelings and refuses every request.','She is a softie with the children because she sympathizes easily and often gives in.','不理会感受且拒绝所有请求，与容易心软相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why does he foster another puppy?','he feels sorry for them and finds it hard to refuse','he dislikes animals','he is a professional snowboarding judge','A softie is easily moved and reluctant to say no.'),Q(1,'Which person might be called a softie?','someone who keeps helping a neighbour in need','someone who ignores every plea','someone who studies sodium','The informal noun describes a tender-hearted person.'),Q(1,'What register does softie have?','informal','highly technical chemistry','a formal legal title','Softie is a colloquial noun.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','Do not be such a softie about giving treats.','The softie is a wall outlet.','She softie the paint.','The first use describes someone who gives in sympathetically.')]);
P('softly','Softly is soft + -ly; it means in a gentle, quiet way and can describe music played or sung at low volume.',[C('softly.s1','quiet movement','She closed the nursery door softly so the baby would remain asleep.','她轻轻关上育婴室的门，以免吵醒宝宝。','closed ... softly','副词修饰 closed，说明动作安静轻柔。','The first sense is in a quiet and gentle way.','第一义是轻轻地、柔和地。'),C('softly.s2','music','The strings entered softly after the opening bars, just as the score instructed.','正如乐谱标记，开头几小节之后弦乐轻柔地进入。','entered softly','音乐中 softly 表示按标记以较低音量演奏或演唱。','The second sense is played or sung at a low volume.','第二义是音乐以低音量轻柔演奏或演唱。')],M('She closed the nursery door softly by slamming it hard enough to wake the baby.','She closed the nursery door softly by moving it quietly and gently.','用力摔门会发出很大声响，与 softly 相反。','usage'),[Q(1,'How did she close the door?','quietly and gently','with a loud slam','while playing a trumpet','Softly describes a gentle quiet action.'),Q(2,'How did the strings play?','at a low volume','at the loudest possible volume','without any instrument','Musical softly is a low-volume direction.'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses softly for manner?','speak softly to the child','a softly cover on the book','softly is a social organization','The adverb modifies the way someone speaks.'),Q(2,'What does a softly played passage sound like?','quiet and gentle','harsh and extremely loud','like falling snow only','The musical sense indicates low volume.')]);
P('softness','Softness is soft + -ness, naming a yielding texture or a gentle quality of voice, light, or character.',C('softness.s1','texture','The softness of the wool surprised the hiker, who had expected the rough fibers to scratch.','羊毛的柔软令徒步者惊讶，因为他原以为粗糙纤维会扎人。','softness of the wool','抽象名词描述触感柔软，也可用于声音、光线或性格的温和。','Softness is a yielding texture or a gentle quality.','softness 指柔软触感或柔和特质。'),M('The softness of the wool surprised him because it was rigid, sharp, and painful to press.','The softness of the wool surprised him because it yielded gently instead of scratching.','坚硬尖锐、按压疼痛与柔软相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What surprised the hiker?','the wool felt gentle rather than scratchy','the wool was made of sodium','the wool formed a snowdrift','Softness describes a yielding texture.'),Q(1,'Which quality can softness describe besides touch?','a gentle voice or light','a numerical age','a social institution only','The noun can refer to gentle sound, light, or character.'),Q(1,'What does -ness form in softness?','a noun naming a quality','an adverb of manner','a past participle','The suffix creates an abstract quality noun.'),Q(1,'Which material has softness?','wool that yields under the hand','a sharp metal edge','a rigid stone wall','The example focuses on tactile softness.')]);
P('software','Software was coined in the 1950s from soft + ware, by contrast with computer hardware; it names programs and data that direct a computer.',C('software.s1','computing','The new software lets the clinic schedule appointments and store test results securely.','新软件使诊所能够安排预约并安全保存检测结果。','software lets the clinic schedule','software 指告诉计算机执行任务的程序和数据。','Software consists of programs and data that tell a computer what to do.','software 是告诉计算机做什么的程序和数据。'),M('The clinic replaced its software with a physical steel keyboard and monitor, neither of which contains programs or data.','The clinic replaced its software with a program that schedules appointments and stores results.','纯物理键盘和显示器属于硬件，不是软件。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What does the clinic use the software for?','scheduling and storing digital records','providing a padded seat','measuring a snowstorm','Software is programs and data used by a computer.'),Q(1,'Which is software?','an appointment-booking program','a physical keyboard','a power socket','The program is intangible computer instruction.'),Q(1,'Why was the term contrasted with hardware?','software names programs and data rather than physical equipment','software is always softer to touch','hardware means a social group','The compound distinguishes digital instructions from physical components.'),Q(1,'What does software tell a computer?','what to do','how to grow sod','how to make a sofa','Programs and data direct computer operations.')]);
P('softwood','Softwood is soft + wood, the timber category from conifers such as pine or spruce; the botanical category contrasts with hardwood and does not guarantee every piece is physically soft.',C('softwood.s1','materials','The frame is made of pine softwood rather than oak hardwood, following the builder’s cost estimate.','按照建筑商的预算，框架用松木软材而不是橡木硬材制作。','pine softwood rather than oak','softwood 是针叶树木材类别，与阔叶树硬材相对。','Softwood is timber from conifers such as pine or spruce.','softwood 指松、云杉等针叶树木材。'),M('The builder called pine softwood because every softwood must be physically softer than every hardwood species.','The builder called pine softwood because it comes from a conifer, though hardness varies among species.','softwood/hardwood 主要按树种分类，并不保证绝对硬度大小。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What kind of tree provides softwood?','a conifer such as pine','a broad-leaved oak','a snowflake','Softwood comes from conifers.'),Q(1,'What distinction is being made between pine and oak?','softwood versus hardwood timber categories','two kinds of software','two types of soda','The term classifies timber by source tree.'),Q(1,'Does softwood always mean physically soft?','no; the category is botanical and hardness varies','yes, every piece is softer than any hardwood','it means the wood is covered in snow','The label refers to conifer timber, not a guaranteed hardness scale.'),Q(1,'Which material is softwood?','spruce timber','oak timber','a flexible book cover','Spruce is a conifer and yields softwood.')]);
P('soil','Soil comes through Anglo-French soil for ground, with its deeper history uncertain; it names earth for plant growth, a country in literary usage, or the act of making something dirty.',[C('soil.s1','gardening','The gardener mixed compost into the soil before planting tomatoes in the raised bed.','园丁在高畦种番茄前，把堆肥混入土壤。','mixed compost into the soil','soil 作名词指地表植物生长的泥土。','The first sense is earth at the surface in which plants grow.','第一义是植物生长的地表土壤。'),C('soil.s2','literary','The soldiers crossed foreign soil after weeks at sea and wrote home as soon as they landed.','士兵们航行数周后踏上异国土地，一登陆便写信回家。','crossed foreign soil','soil 在书面语中可指一个国家的国土。','The second sense is a country, used in literary language.','第二义是书面语中的国土。'),C('soil.s3','cleanliness','The wet clay soiled her white trousers when she knelt beside the garden bed.','她跪在花畦旁时，湿黏土把白裤子弄脏了。','clay soiled her trousers','soil 作及物动词表示弄脏。','The verb means make something dirty.','动词义是使某物变脏。')],M('The wet clay soiled her trousers by leaving them perfectly clean and white.','The wet clay soiled her trousers by leaving dark stains on the fabric.','留下污迹才是弄脏，保持洁白与 soil 的动词义矛盾。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the gardener improve?','the earth in which tomatoes grow','a wall electrical socket','the country’s political borders','Soil in sense 1 is plant-growing earth.'),Q(2,'What does foreign soil mean?','the territory of another country','a gardening mixture','mud on a pair of trousers','The literary use refers to a country or its land.'),Q(3,'What did the clay do to her trousers?','made them dirty','made them softer','made them solar-powered','The verb soil means make dirty.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses soil for growing plants?','The seedlings need rich soil.','He died on foreign soil.','Mud soiled the shoes.','The first use is earth for plant growth.')]);
P('soilage','Soilage is a specialized agricultural term for fresh-cut green forage fed to livestock; the related general noun can also mean the act or result of making something dirty, and the formation history is uncertain.',[C('soilage.s1','agriculture','The dairy herd received fresh soilage each morning, cut from the rye field just before feeding.','奶牛每天早晨都吃新割的青饲料，这些饲料在喂食前刚从黑麦田割下。','received fresh soilage','农业义指割下后即喂牲畜的新鲜青绿饲料。','Soilage can mean fresh green forage cut and fed to livestock.','soilage 可指割下后喂牲畜的新鲜青饲料。'),C('soilage.s1','cleaning','The report noted soilage on the uniform sleeve after the worker knelt beside the muddy pump.','报告记录了工人在泥泵旁跪下后，制服袖口沾上的污迹。','soilage on the uniform sleeve','同一词也可指弄脏的情况或结果。','The noun can also refer to the act or result of soiling.','该名词也可指弄脏这一情况或结果。')],M('The farm called dry plastic feed bags soilage even though no green forage had been cut or fed to livestock.','The farm called freshly cut rye fed directly to its cows soilage.','农业义的 soilage 是青饲料，不是干塑料包装袋。','word-choice'),[Q(1,'What did the dairy herd receive?','freshly cut green forage','dry plastic feed bags','a bottle of soft drink','The agricultural sense is fresh forage fed to animals.'),Q(1,'When was the rye cut?','just before it was fed','after it had become a wooden frame','only after snowfall in summer','Soilage is generally cut fresh for feeding.'),Q(1,'What did the report note on the sleeve?','a dirty mark or soilage','fresh livestock forage','a solar panel','The noun can also name dirt or the act/result of soiling.'),Q(1,'Which context uses soilage as farm feed?','fresh green cuttings given to cattle','a stain left on a uniform','earth where tomatoes grow','The agricultural use refers to cut forage.')]);
P('soilless','Soilless is soil + -less, “without soil”; it describes growing methods such as hydroponics that use water or another medium instead.',C('soilless.s1','horticulture','The greenhouse uses soilless culture, feeding lettuce roots with a carefully measured nutrient solution.','温室采用无土栽培，用精确配比的营养液供给生菜根部。','soilless culture','-less 表示没有土壤，仍可用水或其他介质培养植物。','Soilless means grown or practised without soil, as in hydroponics.','soilless 指不使用土壤种植，如水培。'),M('The greenhouse called its method soilless while growing every lettuce plant directly in deep field soil.','The greenhouse used a soilless method by growing lettuce roots in nutrient solution without soil.','直接在土壤中种植与 soilless 的定义矛盾。','distinction'),[Q(1,'How did the greenhouse feed lettuce?','with a nutrient solution rather than soil','by planting it in deep field soil','with a soft drink','Soilless culture grows plants without soil.'),Q(1,'Which method is soilless?','hydroponics','planting directly in a garden bed','laying sod on a lawn','Hydroponics is a soil-free growing method.'),Q(1,'What does -less mean in soilless?','without','full of','able to use','The suffix signals absence of soil.'),Q(1,'Can plants grow in a soilless system?','yes, using water or another growing medium','no, the word means no plants can live','only if planted in soil','The adjective describes the method, not an inability to grow.')]);
P('sojourn','Sojourn came from Old French sojorner, “stay for a time,” from Latin subdiurnare, “spend the day”; it is both a temporary stay and the act of staying.',[C('sojourn.s1','travel','Her month-long sojourn in Kyoto included language classes and daily visits to a neighbourhood market.','她在京都逗留一个月，期间上语言课，每天去附近市场。','month-long sojourn','名词指在非家乡地点的短暂停留。','A sojourn is a short stay in a place that is not your home.','sojourn 作名词指在非家乡的地方短暂停留。'),C('sojourn.s2','travel','During the repairs, the family sojourned with relatives on the coast.','房屋维修期间，这家人暂住在海边的亲戚家。','sojourned with relatives','sojourn 作动词表示在某处住一段时间。','The verb means stay in a place for a time.','动词义是在某处暂住一段时间。')],M('Their sojourn with relatives lasted only briefly, but the sentence says they never stayed there at all.','Their sojourn with relatives lasted briefly while repairs were completed.','sojourn 表示确有一段暂住，不能说从未停留。','meaning'),[Q(1,'How long was her stay in Kyoto?','one month','several years permanently','one afternoon only','A sojourn is a temporary stay, here lasting a month.'),Q(2,'Where did the family stay during repairs?','with relatives on the coast','in a snowdrift','at a soccer stadium','The verb means stay temporarily in a place.'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses sojourn as a noun?','a brief sojourn abroad','they sojourned in Rome','sojourn the house softly','The first phrase names the temporary stay.'),Q(2,'Which sentence uses sojourn as a verb?','We sojourned in the village for a week.','Our sojourn ended on Friday.','The sojourn was peaceful.','The first sentence describes the act of staying.')]);
P('solar','Solar comes from Latin solaris, “of the sun,” from sol “sun”; it describes something related to the sun or powered by its energy.',[C('solar.s1','astronomy','Earth is the third planet in the solar system, orbiting the Sun with seven other planets.','地球是太阳系的第三颗行星，与其他七颗行星一起绕太阳运行。','solar system','太阳义形容词表示与太阳有关。','The first sense means of or from the Sun.','第一义是属于太阳或来自太阳的。'),C('solar.s2','energy','The school installed solar panels to turn sunlight into electricity for its classrooms.','学校安装了太阳能板，把阳光转化为教室用电。','solar panels','太阳能义强调利用太阳能量，而不只是与太阳有关。','The second sense means using energy from the Sun.','第二义是利用太阳能量的。')],M('The school installed solar panels that generated electricity without using or receiving any energy from sunlight.','The school installed solar panels that converted sunlight into electricity.','太阳能板利用阳光发电；完全不接收阳光的装置不属此义。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What does solar system refer to?','the Sun and objects orbiting it','a set of softwood boards','a group of social clubs','Solar in sense 1 means relating to the Sun.'),Q(2,'What do the panels do?','convert sunlight into electricity','block all sunlight from reaching the school','soften the classroom walls','Solar in the energy sense means powered by sunlight.'),Q(1,'Which use is about the Sun generally?','a solar eclipse','a solar-powered pump','a soft drink','An eclipse is an astronomical event involving the Sun.'),Q(2,'Which phrase specifically means using solar energy?','solar-powered equipment','solar system','solar orbit','The second sense concerns harnessing sunlight as energy.')]);
P('solar-powered','Solar-powered combines solar + powered, the past participle of power; it describes a device driven by electricity or heat obtained from sunlight.',C('solar-powered.s1','technology','A solar-powered pump lifted water to the storage tank even when the village generator was offline.','即使村里的发电机停机，太阳能水泵仍把水抽进储水箱。','solar-powered pump','复合形容词说明设备由阳光转化的电或热驱动。','Solar-powered means powered by electricity or heat obtained from sunlight.','solar-powered 指靠阳光转化的电或热来驱动。'),M('The solar-powered pump worked through the night in a sealed room with no sunlight or stored solar energy.','The solar-powered pump ran on electricity stored from the solar panels during daylight.','没有阳光且没有储存太阳能时，设备不能靠太阳能驱动。','context'),[Q(1,'How did the pump run while the generator was offline?','on electricity obtained from sunlight','on a hand crank only','on a soft drink','Solar-powered devices use energy derived from sunlight.'),Q(1,'Which item is solar-powered?','a calculator whose panel converts light to electricity','a battery-only device with no solar input','a wooden sofa','The adjective describes equipment driven by solar energy.'),Q(1,'What does powered indicate in the compound?','the energy source driving the device','the device’s color','that it is made of wood','Powered identifies what supplies operating energy.'),Q(1,'When could the pump still run at night?','when it uses energy stored from sunlight during the day','when it receives no energy of any kind','when it is connected to a snowstorm','Stored solar electricity can power it after sunset.')]);
})();
